E["item:gnoam-sprecklesprocket"] = {t="item",n="Gnoam Sprecklesprocket",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Gnoam Sprecklesprocket powers a plan to reach Gnomeregan. Shoni the Shilent seeks it for drilling machines that could breach the rock around the lost gnomish home.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Gnoam Sprecklesprocket powers a plan to reach Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Vital Power Source",b="Sneed's shredder runs deep in the Defias stronghold. The goblin taskmaster Sneed pilots the machine, whose compact power core supplies energy for heavy logging and cutting blades. Its steady output makes the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket valuable salvage in the tunnels of Westfall.",sp=0},{t="Breaching Gnomeregan",b="In Stormwind City, the gnomish inventor Shoni the Shilent has chosen the Deadmines shredder for a larger effort. Gnomish forces seek to reclaim Gnomeregan from the troggs who overran it, but sealed underground approaches block the way. Shoni plans to power heavy gyrodrillmatic excavationators with the Sprecklesprocket. They could bore through the bedrock around the lost techno-city and open an unexpected route for an underground assault.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is a high-output power supply taken from a goblin shredder deep in the Deadmines. It can run heavy underground drilling machines.",al={"sprecklesprocket","what is this sprocket","what is the item"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket come from?",a="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket comes from Sneed's Shredder, an industrial lumber machine operated by the goblin taskmaster Sneed in the Deadmines lumber mills.",al={"who drops it","how to get sprecklesprocket","shredder drop"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Shoni the Shilent need it?",a="Shoni the Shilent needs the sprocket to power gyrodrillmatic excavationators. The machines can bore through the rock around Gnomeregan, opening a route for gnomes aligned with the Alliance to assault the troggs.",al={"why does shoni want this","shoni quest item"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the sprocket goblin or gnomish technology?",a="The sprocket comes from a working goblin shredder in the Deadmines, and Shoni plans to use it in gnomish drilling machinery. No one says who first designed the component.",al={"is it goblin tech","gnome or goblin device"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each salvaged component brings you closer to drilling into your lost home and driving out the troggs.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how this intact power supply could run the machinery needed to bore through Gnomeregan's underground rock barriers."},kw={"deadmines","gnoam sprecklesprocket","gnomeregan","gyrodrillmatic","shoni the shilent","sneed","sneed's shredder","sprecklesprocket"},rel={"quest:2040","npc:sneed-s-shredder","npc:shoni-the-shilent","npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","zone:gnomeregan","topic:trogg"},src={"Gnoam Sprecklesprocket","Underground Assault"}}
E["item:head-of-vancleef"] = {t="item",n="Head of VanCleef",z="deadmines",s="At Sentinel Hill, VanCleef's severed head proves the Defias leader has fallen. Carried from the depths of the Deadmines, it brings the People's Militia hard-won vengeance.",h="At Sentinel Hill, VanCleef's severed head proves the Defias leader has fallen.",sec={{t="Proof of the Master's Fall",b="Westfall's settlers need proof that their danger has passed. For months, Edwin VanCleef directed the Defias Brotherhood's terror from the deepest sanctum of the Deadmines, guarded by armed outlaws, goblin engineers, and a massive war juggernaut. Gryan Stoutmantle, leader of the People's Militia, demands physical proof before declaring the countryside safe. VanCleef's severed head, brought out into daylight, assures the exhausted defenders that the architect of their ruin can no longer threaten Westfall.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Victory",b="VanCleef's death answers Stoutmantle's call for Westfall's good, but the sight of his head carries solemn weight. He was once the revered master builder who rebuilt Stormwind after the First War. Betrayal and unpaid debts drove him and the Stonemasons Guild into outlaw rebellion. His death marks the end of the local militia's campaign and exposes the kingdom's failure to settle its own domestic turmoil. Volunteer farmers and foreign adventurers have been left to carry out high justice.",sp=1,bt={"defias.masons"}}},faq={{q="Who wants the Head of VanCleef?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle, captain of the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill in Westfall, wants the head to bring the long campaign against the Defias Brotherhood to its close.",al={"who do i turn this into","who takes vancleef head","where does vancleef head go"}},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle demand his head specifically?",a="The Defias Brotherhood held Westfall under its grip for so long that rumors of VanCleef's death would not convince the people. Stoutmantle needs physical proof to reassure the beleaguered farmers and show that the militia's struggle was not in vain.",al={"why take his head","why vancleef head"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the head obtained?",a="The head is taken from Edwin VanCleef aboard his secret ironclad warship, at the very end of the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook in southwestern Westfall.",al={"where to get vancleef head","how to get head of vancleef"},it="origin"},{q="Does taking VanCleef's head end the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Stoutmantle sees VanCleef's death as the beginning of the end for the brotherhood. Splinter groups, rogue bandits, and sympathizers still linger throughout Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and beyond.",al={"is defias destroyed","what happens to the defias"}},{q="What is the Head of VanCleef?",a="The Head of VanCleef is the severed head of Edwin VanCleef, the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood hiding deep inside the Deadmines. It serves as gruesome, indisputable proof that the leader of the outlaw uprising has finally been brought down.",al={"what is head of vancleef","head of vancleef item","edwin vancleef head"},it="identity",add="4a1d52aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="VanCleef's head brings the People's Militia a cathartic victory, while exposing the troubling absence of the Stormwind House of Nobles during Westfall's darkest hour.",["class:Rogue"]="Edwin VanCleef was one of the deadliest rogue masters in human history. His death ends a peerless career in shadows and sabotage."},kw={"deadmines","edwin vancleef","gryan stoutmantle","head of vancleef","peoples militia","sentinel hill","westfall"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","quest:65","zone:deadmines","zone:westfall","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:12","topic:alliance"},src={"Head of VanCleef","The Defias Brotherhood (7)"}}
E["item:miners-union-card"] = {t="item",n="Miners' Union Card",z="deadmines",s="In Moonbrook, union cards mark the laborers lost beneath the earth. Workers once carried them through the mines, and now the cards remain with skeletal dead in the dark drifts.",h="In Moonbrook, union cards mark the laborers lost beneath the earth.",sec={{t="Tragedy in the Deep",b="Before the Defias Brotherhood took control of Moonbrook, miners worked below ground for the guild, drawing valuable ore for the kingdom. A tunnel collapse crushed a major shaft and killed dozens beneath the rock. The dead rose as skeletal miners, excavators, and dynamiters. Union cards remain in their bony pockets, the last proof of who they were. In Stormwind, surviving colleagues seek the cards to learn the dead workers' identities and bring closure to their families.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Miners' Union Card?",a="A Miners' Union Card identified a member of the guild that worked the Moonbrook mines. Surviving workers use the cards to learn who died in the cave-in.",al={"what is union card","miners card","union card"},it="identity"},{q="Where do these cards come from?",a="The cards are found on undead laborers in the collapsed drifts beneath Moonbrook, including skeletal miners, undead excavators, and undead dynamiters.",al={"where to find union cards","who drops miners cards","card drop location"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the miners undead?",a="A cave-in sealed the miners in a deep shaft. What raised them as undead is unknown; their remains now haunt the collapsed drifts beneath Moonbrook.",al={"why skeletal miners","how did miners die","deadmines undead"}},{q="Who wants these cards returned?",a="Surviving co-workers who escaped the cave-in and now live in Stormwind City seek the cards. They hope to tell the fallen miners' families what happened and bring them peace.",al={"who takes union cards","collecting memories questgiver","turn in union cards"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="For prospectors and miners, these cards recall the deadly risks of cave-ins and mine shafts left unmanaged.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering the cards can bring closure to families across the kingdom of Stormwind who never learned what became of their working kin."},kw={"cave-in","collecting memories","deadmines","miners' union card","moonbrook","skeletal miner","stormwind","union card"},rel={"quest:168","subzone:deadmines","zone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Miners' Union Card","Collecting Memories"}}
E["item:thistlenettle-s-badge"] = {t="item",n="Thistlenettle's Badge",z="deadmines",s="Foreman Thistlenettle's badge is all that remains after the collapse in the Deadmines.",h="Foreman Thistlenettle's badge is all that remains after the collapse in the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Explorers' League in the Deadmines",b="Before the Defias Brotherhood sealed Moonbrook and the tunnels beneath it, dwarven prospectors from Ironforge's Explorers' League worked the old gold mines of Westfall. Foreman Thistlenettle and his crew were deep underground when a tunnel collapsed and split them apart. His brother Wilder escaped to Stormwind City, but the foreman and several laborers were left trapped below.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Foreman Thistlenettle died in the unsealed tunnels and rose as mindless undead among the collapsed shafts outside the main foundry. His Explorers' League Badge remained with him. Recovered and brought to his grieving brother, it proves the foreman's death.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who does this badge belong to?",a="The badge belonged to Foreman Thistlenettle, a dwarven miner and member of the Explorers' League. A sudden tunnel collapse trapped him deep underground beneath Westfall.",al={"who owned thistlenettle badge","thistlenettle badge owner"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the badge found?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle carries the badge in the monster-infested upper corridors of the Deadmines, outside the main entrance to the Defias stronghold.",al={"badge location","how to get thistlenettles badge","where to find thistlenettle"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants Thistlenettle's Badge?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle wants the badge. He is the foreman's brother and lives in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, awaiting word of his kin's fate.",al={"who takes thistlenettles badge","who turns in oh brother","wilder thistlenettle location"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why were the Thistlenettle brothers in the Deadmines?",a="The brothers surveyed and prospected the mineral-rich caverns beneath Moonbrook for the Explorers' League. Hostile thieves and tunnel collapses ruined their expedition.",al={"why were dwarves in deadmines","thistlenettle deadmines mission"},it="history"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know Foreman Thistlenettle carried the Explorers' League badge into Westfall. Recovering it keeps a fallen son of Ironforge from being forgotten.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can bring closure to a grieving dwarf in Stormwind's Dwarven District."},kw={"deadmines","explorers' league","moonbrook","oh brother","thistlenettle","thistlenettle's badge","westfall","wilder"},rel={"quest:167","npc:foreman-thistlenettle","npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","topic:explorers-league","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Thistlenettle's Badge","Oh Brother. . ."}}
E["npc:captain-greenskin"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Greenskin",z="deadmines",s="In the Deadmines cove, Captain Greenskin readies a warship for Edwin VanCleef. The goblin pirate oversees its crew and construction for the Defias Brotherhood, preparing the ironclad juggernaut to sail against Stormwind.",h="In the Deadmines cove, Captain Greenskin readies a warship for Edwin VanCleef.",sec={{t="Master of the Juggernaut",b="Captain Greenskin paces the main deck of the juggernaut under construction in the Deadmines cove. A seasoned goblin mariner, he was brought into Edwin VanCleef's inner circle to turn an underground cavern into a drydock for a warship.",sp=0},{t="A Pirate's Crew",b="Captain Greenskin commands cutthroats, not stonemasons or bandits. His crew includes Mr. Smite, his fearsome tauren first mate, and Cookie, the murloc ship's cook. Together, they hold the gangplanks and upper deck, guarding the way to VanCleef's private cabin atop the bridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Greenskin?",a="Captain Greenskin is a goblin pirate captain hired by Edwin VanCleef to oversee the completion and operation of the Defias Brotherhood's secret warship in the Deadmines.",al={"greenskin lore","who is greenskin","captain greenskin"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Greenskin come from before joining the Defias?",a="No record tells where Greenskin sailed before entering VanCleef's pay. He commands the Defias juggernaut and its crew in the Deadmines.",al={"greenskin origin","where is greenskin from","greenskin booty bay"},it="origin"},{q="Who serves under Captain Greenskin?",a="Greenskin commands Mr. Smite, his tauren first mate, Cookie, the murloc cook, and Defias pirates patrolling the ironclad's deck.",al={"greenskin crew","first mate","greenskin minions"},it="ties"},{q="What is Greenskin's purpose in the Deadmines?",a="Greenskin is charged with making the massive ironclad warship seaworthy and ready to sail from the underground cove into the Great Sea against Stormwind.",al={"what does greenskin do","why is greenskin here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Captain Greenskin be found?",a="Captain Greenskin paces the main deck of the large juggernaut anchored in the final cavern of the Deadmines, guarding the approach to Edwin VanCleef.",al={"greenskin location","where is captain greenskin"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is Captain Greenskin part of the Defias Brotherhood or a mercenary?",a="Captain Greenskin is a mercenary pirate captain in Edwin VanCleef's direct employ, commanding the naval forces aligned with the Defias Brotherhood's plot.",al={"is greenskin defias","greenskin faction"},it="side"},{q="Why is Captain Greenskin here?",a="Captain Greenskin was hired by Edwin VanCleef to oversee the construction and command of the Defias Brotherhood's massive juggernaut. He remains aboard the vessel deep within the Deadmines cove, directing his pirate crew and making sure the warship is completed and armed.",al={"why is greenskin in deadmines","captain greenskin why here","greenskin deadmines purpose"},it="why_here",add="9c1c4117"},{q="What does Captain Greenskin want?",a="As a hired goblin captain, Greenskin seeks profit and the thrill of naval command. He intends to finish constructing the colossal ironclad warship in the Deadmines cove and captain it out into the Great Sea in service to Edwin VanCleef's schemes against Stormwind.",al={"greenskin goal","what does captain greenskin want","greenskin motive"},it="wants",add="6bcae29e"},{q="Why is Captain Greenskin feared?",a="Captain Greenskin commands the pirate crew of Edwin VanCleef's juggernaut, backed by brutal raiders like his tauren first mate, Mr. Smite. Pacing the deck with a cleaving blade and poisoned harpoons, he stands between intruders and VanCleef himself.",al={"why is greenskin feared","captain greenskin reputation","is greenskin famous"},it="fame",add="433e5911"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Captain Greenskin commands the Defias rebellion's maritime threat. If his juggernaut reaches the coast, Westfall and Stormwind's undefended shores are at direct risk.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find Greenskin at the head of Defias piracy, heavily guarded by corsairs and brutes on the warship's deck."},kw={"captain greenskin","deadmines","goblin pirate","greenskin","juggernaut","smite","vancleef"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:mr-smite","npc:cookie","zone:deadmines","topic:pirate","topic:goblin","topic:alliance"},src={"Captain Greenskin"}}
E["npc:cookie"] = {t="npc",n="Cookie",z="deadmines",s="Cookie tends the crew's cauldrons aboard the juggernaut deep in the Deadmines. A murloc among the Defias Brotherhood, he cooks beneath the watch of Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef. In the underground dry dock, he is the only entirely optional boss.",h="Cookie tends the crew's cauldrons aboard the juggernaut deep in the Deadmines.",sec={{t="The Brotherhood's Chef",b="Cookie cooks beneath the decks of the towering juggernaut in Ironclad Cove. No human outrider or goblin engineer takes the duty; the solitary murloc does. How Cookie came to hold the position is unknown. The rest of the crew may doubt a murloc's cooking, but pirates rarely choose their meals with care. In Moonbrook's underworld, a meal is a meal.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Brew",b="Cookie patrols the waterways and shores around the pirate flagship. He wields cooking utensils and throws acidic brews. Though apart from typical murloc tribes, he defends his cauldron with savage force, flinging caustic mixtures at intruders who enter the docks. His station lies away from the main gangplanks, so many who storm the cove pass his kitchen by. Cookie is the only overseer aboard the Defias juggernaut who can be bypassed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a murloc working as a cook for the Defias?",a="No record explains how Cookie came to serve aboard the juggernaut. Defias outlaws and goblin shipwrights accept the arrangement because pirate crews take food where they can get it, whatever the cook's species.",al={"why murloc cook","why is cookie on the ship","cookie defias lore"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can Cookie be found in the Deadmines?",a="Cookie is at Ironclad Cove, at the very end of the Deadmines. He patrols the shallow water and docks near the stern of the giant wooden juggernaut, just past the ramp guarded by Mr. Smite.",al={"where is cookie","cookie location deadmines","finding cookie"},gp=true},{q="Is Cookie required to finish the Deadmines?",a="No, Cookie is the only optional boss in the Deadmines. Infiltrators can board the vessel and confront Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef without disturbing the cook's patrol along the shore.",al={"is cookie optional","do you have to kill cookie","cookie skip"},gp=true},{q="Does Cookie belong to a specific murloc tribe?",a="Cookie is not associated with any known local murloc tribe, including those along the Westfall coast. He lives and works among the outlaws and scoundrels of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what tribe is cookie","cookie murloc tribe"},it="origin"},{q="What weapons or attacks does Cookie use?",a="Cookie fights at close range with cooking implements and hurls caustic splashes of acid at attackers, burning them with dangerous culinary mixtures.",al={"cookie abilities","how does cookie fight","cookie attacks"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Who does Cookie report to on the juggernaut?",a="Cookie serves the naval arm of the Defias Brotherhood under Captain Greenskin's command, and ultimately answers to Edwin VanCleef.",al={"cookie boss","who leads cookie","cookie greenskin vancleef"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Cookie?",a="Cookie is an elite murloc serving as the ship's cook aboard Edwin VanCleef's ironclad juggernaut deep within the Deadmines. Unlike most feral murlocs encountered wandering the shores of Westfall, Cookie has found an unusual home among human outlaws, preparing questionable meals over his cauldron for the Defias Brotherhood's pirate crew.",al={"who is cookie","cookie identity","who is the murloc chef"},it="identity",add="f44f954f"},{q="Whose side is Cookie on?",a="Cookie is firmly loyal to the Defias Brotherhood. Stationed on the juggernaut alongside Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef, he serves the outlaw pirates directly and will fiercely defend the ship against any Alliance intruders seeking to disrupt VanCleef's rebellion.",al={"cookie allegiance","is cookie defias","what faction is cookie"},it="side",add="c6e0c482"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Finding a murloc as chief cook aboard an outlaw juggernaut speaks to the desperate, unrefined standards of pirate cuisine.",["class:Rogue"]="VanCleef's rogue network relies on strange, unconventional assets. Cookie is one of the odd surprises in the Brotherhood's supply lines.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind's scouts may be surprised to find murlocs working within Defias leadership, rather than only along Westfall's outer shores."},kw={"captain greenskin","cook","cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaut","murloc"},rel={"npc:captain-greenskin","npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:mr-smite","zone:deadmines","topic:murloc","topic:pirate"},src={"Cookie"}}
E["npc:edwin-vancleef"] = {t="npc",n="Edwin VanCleef",z="deadmines",s="In the Deadmines, brilliant Edwin VanCleef commands the Defias Brotherhood. He once led the Stonemasons who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Second War. The House of Nobles denied the workers their promised pay, and VanCleef now seeks vengeance against the kingdom he helped restore.",h="In the Deadmines, brilliant Edwin VanCleef commands the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="Architect of the Kingdom",b="Edwin VanCleef led the Stonemasons Guild as it rebuilt Stormwind City after the First War. A peerless craftsman and idealist, he mastered architecture and directed the building of the capital's grand ramparts and towering cathedrals. His childhood friend Mathias Shaw trained him in stealth, subterfuge, and bladecraft, making VanCleef a deadly operative as well as a master architect.",sp=0},{t="The Riot and the Brotherhood",b="After years of labor, the Stonemasons finished rebuilding Stormwind. The House of Nobles had run up colossal debts through military campaigns and refused the guild its promised compensation. VanCleef demanded restitution, but the nobles dissolved the guild. He led the workers in a riot and out of the city. In the chaos, his lieutenant and most trusted assistant, Bazil Thredd, was captured and left in the Stockade. In Westfall, VanCleef gathered the exiled workers and allied outcasts under the Defias Brotherhood's banner.",sp=0},{t="Retribution from the Shadows",b="The Defias drove Westfall's farmers from their homes and claimed its rich gold deposits while the crown neglected the countryside. Deep in Moonbrook's Deadmines, VanCleef directs the building of a massive juggernaut warship for an armed assault on Stormwind. The House of Nobles dismisses the thieves as disorganized brigands, while VanCleef has joined forces with river crooks, gnolls, and pirates. His embittered labor union has become an army poised against the monarchy.",sp=1,bt={"defias.juggernaut"}}},faq={{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef leads the Defias Brotherhood and once served as Guildmaster of the Stonemasons. He is the master architect who rebuilt Stormwind City after the Horde destroyed it during the First War.",al={"who is vancleef","edwin vancleef lore","vancleef identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why did the Stonemasons revolt against Stormwind?",a="After the Stonemasons rebuilt Stormwind City, the House of Nobles refused to pay the guild its agreed wages because the kingdom was deeply in debt. VanCleef and the workers protested, but the nobles disbanded the guild, and violent riots broke out in the streets.",al={"why did defias rebel","why did stonemasons riot","reason for defias riot"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Edwin VanCleef hiding?",a="Edwin VanCleef commands the Defias Brotherhood from the innermost sanctum of the Deadmines in Westfall. The entrance is rumored to lie through the quiet village of Moonbrook.",al={"where is vancleef","vancleef location","deadmines boss location"},sp=1,it="why_here",bt={"defias.hideout"}},{q="What is his connection to Mathias Shaw?",a="Mathias Shaw was Edwin VanCleef's childhood friend. Shaw trained VanCleef in stealth, thievery, and combat, hoping he would join the royal intelligence agency SI:7.",al={"vancleef and shaw","is vancleef related to shaw","mathias shaw friend"},it="ties"},{q="What happened to Bazil Thredd during the riot?",a="During the riots, VanCleef's lieutenant and most trusted assistant, Bazil Thredd, was captured and held in prison. While VanCleef led the Stonemasons out of the city, Thredd was all but forgotten in the Stockade as he awaited trial and questioning.",al={"who is bazil thredd","vancleef lieutenant","bazil thredd riot"},it="history"},{q="What is he building in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias have conscripted clever goblins to help build something terrible at the bottom of the Deadmines, but what it may be remains uncertain.",al={"deadmines ship","what is inside deadmines","vancleef warship"},sp=1,it="purpose",bt={"defias.juggernaut"}},{q="Whose side is Edwin VanCleef on?",a="Edwin VanCleef stands solely with the Defias Brotherhood, the rebel syndicate he founded from the outcasts of the former Stonemasons Guild. He opposes both the House of Nobles and the crown of Stormwind, holding the entire kingdom responsible for breaking faith with his craftsmen. He owes no loyalty to the Alliance or the Horde, operating as an outlaw mastermind bent on pursuing his own fierce war of vengeance.",al={"edwin vancleef allegiance","who does edwin vancleef fight for","is vancleef alliance or horde"},it="side",add="7e824b42"},{q="What does Edwin VanCleef want?",a="VanCleef seeks total retribution against the Kingdom of Stormwind. After spending years rebuilding the capital city only to have the corrupt House of Nobles refuse payment and strip the Stonemasons Guild of their livelihood, he swore that the entire kingdom would pay for their betrayal. He aims to breach the city's defenses, crush the aristocracy, and exact vengeance for his exiled craftsmen through armed rebellion and open devastation.",al={"vancleef goal","what is edwin vancleef's goal","why is vancleef attacking stormwind"},it="wants",add="01cc4ddf"},{q="Why is Edwin VanCleef so feared?",a="Stormwind considers VanCleef one of the greatest perils to its security because he combines brilliant architectural knowledge with lethal rogue training. Having designed the very fortifications protecting the capital, he knows every vulnerability in the kingdom's defenses. Backed by a vast, cutthroat criminal network and heavily fortified within the Deadmines, he commands enough firepower, manpower, and cunning to bring the boy-king's realm to its knees.",al={"why is vancleef famous","why is edwin vancleef feared","edwin vancleef threat"},it="fame",add="5f8574b7"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, VanCleef's story shows the cost of the kingdom's postwar recovery: a loyal hero whose own livelihood was denied, turning him into the realm's deadliest insurgent.",["class:Rogue"]="Mathias Shaw, the leader of SI:7, trained VanCleef himself. VanCleef became one of Azeroth's most capable rogues, combining guild leadership with elite assassination techniques.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders see VanCleef as the leading internal security threat to southern human lands. His actions paralyze Westfall and the borders of Elwynn Forest."},kw={"brotherhood","deadmines","defias","moonbrook","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:stonemasons-guild","zone:deadmines","zone:westfall","npc:mathias-shaw","npc:baros-alexston","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","quest:373"},src={"Edwin VanCleef"}}
E["npc:gilnid"] = {t="npc",n="Gilnid",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Gilnid runs the goblin forges for the Defias Brotherhood. Known as the Smelter, he oversees the work that turns raw ore into refined metal and munitions for Edwin VanCleef's hidden ironclad juggernaut. His foundry makes the heavy cannons the Brotherhood needs to strike Stormwind.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Gilnid runs the goblin forges for the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="Master of the Foundry",b="Deep in the Deadmines, the Defias Brotherhood depends on skilled hands to forge its weapons of war. Gilnid, VanCleef's head smelter, commands goblin laborers, tinkers, and smiths in the central foundry. Taller than most of his kin, he drives them through smoke and slag, barking orders and allowing no breaks. Their work turns raw iron ore into heavy plating and deadly ordnance.",sp=0},{t="Arming the Juggernaut",b="Gilnid's foundry feeds the Brotherhood's great ambition. He oversees the heavy cannons and ammunition meant for the colossal ironclad warship docked in a subterranean cove beyond his workshop. The Defias vessel cannot make its planned strike against Stormwind until his crew has forged every gun, barrel, and ball.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gilnid?",a="Gilnid is a goblin engineer and Edwin VanCleef's head smelter in the Deadmines. He oversees the Brotherhood's forges and directs the work of casting cannons and ammunition for its war machine.",al={"gilnid deadmines","who is gilnid","the smelter"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gilnid in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood hired goblin engineers to build and supply its hidden warship. Gilnid leads the smelting works, turning mined iron ore into refined parts, armor, and artillery.",al={"why is a goblin in deadmines","gilnid defias lore","what is gilnid doing"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Gilnid working on?",a="Gilnid oversees the cannons, ship parts, and shot needed to arm the juggernaut hidden in the docks deeper inside the mines.",al={"gilnid cannon","what is gilnid building","deadmines forge purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why must Gilnid be defeated?",a="Gilnid controls the foundry blocking the way to the cove. The heavy blast doors deeper in the mines remain sealed until the smelting room is secured.",al={"why kill gilnid","door past gilnid"},it="danger"},{q="Does Gilnid work directly for Edwin VanCleef?",a="Yes. Gilnid is a contracted goblin specialist who serves directly under VanCleef, handling heavy metalwork and weapons production. He was not one of the original Stonemasons.",al={"vancleef and gilnid","is gilnid defias leader"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there so many goblins around him?",a="Gilnid leads a goblin engineering crew in the foundry. They operate the blast furnaces, pour molten iron, and assemble ordnance under his strict supervision.",al={"gilnid goblins","deadmines forge crew"},it="people"},{q="Whose side is Gilnid on?",a="Gilnid is firmly aligned with the Defias Brotherhood. While goblins are typically known for their independent mercenary contracts and neutrality, Gilnid has committed his formidable metallurgical talents to Edwin VanCleef's rebellious cause, serving as a chief overseer deep within the brotherhood's underground stronghold.",al={"gilnid faction","gilnid defias brotherhood","who does gilnid fight for"},it="side",add="1c6d7566"},{q="What does Gilnid want?",a="Gilnid wants nothing more than to see the Defias juggernaut fully equipped and operational. As head smelter, his overriding drive is ensuring that every last cannon, casing, and round of heavy ammunition is forged to perfection, driving his goblin laborers mercilessly without rest until the massive warship is ready to sail.",al={"gilnid goal","what is gilnid trying to do","gilnid motivation"},it="wants",add="88f08ccf"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Gilnid's blast furnaces and smelting pots show how the Defias Brotherhood turns Westfall's raw minerals into refined iron and weapons.",["profession:Engineering"]="Gilnid's foundry shows goblin heavy industry at work, producing naval cannons, ammunition, and structural plating under harsh conditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stopping Gilnid shuts down the Defias weapons line and keeps VanCleef's warship from being fully armed to threaten Stormwind Harbor."},kw={"cannons","deadmines","defias","forge","foundry","gilnid","goblin","juggernaut","smelter","vancleef"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:goblin","quest:65"},src={"Gilnid"}}
E["npc:miner-johnson"] = {t="npc",n="Miner Johnson",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Miner Johnson wanders among the Defias laborers. He is a seasoned miner who oversees excavation ahead of the heavy machinery, though he appears only now and then.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Miner Johnson wanders among the Defias laborers.",sec={{t="A Rare Face in the Deep",b="Miner Johnson works among the laborers digging beneath the Deadmines for Edwin VanCleef's hidden fortress. He waits in an alcove to the left, before the shredders in the Mast Room. Stronger and more aggressive than the other miners, he can be hard to find as he wanders the tunnels.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Defias War Machine",b="Beneath Moonbrook, the Defias Brotherhood needs ore for weapons, reinforced shafts, and mechanical contraptions. Johnson and the other miners dig the mineral seams beneath Westfall. Anyone who enters his work area will find that he guards it fiercely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Miner Johnson?",a="Miner Johnson is a human miner allied with the Defias Brotherhood. He works in a side alcove among other laborers, before the goblin shredder deep in the Deadmines.",al={"miner johnson lore","who is miner johnson","deadmines miner johnson"},it="identity"},{q="Where exactly is Miner Johnson located?",a="Johnson works in the upper shafts of the Deadmines, before the room where Sneed and his shredder are found. Look for a small alcove to the left, where miners chip at the rock.",al={"miner johnson location","where is miner johnson","how to find miner johnson"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why isn't Miner Johnson always there?",a="Miner Johnson appears only occasionally in the Deadmines. Most groups find an ordinary miner in his place.",al={"miner johnson not spawning","is miner johnson rare","miner johnson spawn rate"},gp=true},{q="Is Miner Johnson part of any quest?",a="Miner Johnson has no formal bounty. He is an unexpected encounter for parties exploring the Deadmines.",al={"miner johnson quest","does miner johnson have a quest"},gp=true},{q="What is Miner Johnson's role in the Deadmines?",a="Miner Johnson helps the Defias Brotherhood dig up metal, stone, and other resources for its underground base and hidden juggernaut.",al={"what does miner johnson do","miner johnson role"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Miner Johnson dangerous compared to other miners?",a="Yes. Miner Johnson is much tougher and hits harder than the ordinary miners. A group must work together to bring him down safely.",al={"how hard is miner johnson","is miner johnson elite"},it="danger"},{q="Whose side is Miner Johnson on?",a="He stands with the Defias Brotherhood and their workforce. Toiling deep inside the Deadmines alongside the other laborers, Miner Johnson shares their allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's uprising, wielding his pick against any intruders who breach their subterranean stronghold.",al={"miner johnson faction","who does miner johnson work for","is miner johnson defias"},it="side",add="3a6e6cc9"},{q="Why is Miner Johnson in the Deadmines?",a="He works in a small alcove off the mine tunnels, just before the shredder, digging out gold and iron for the Defias Brotherhood. Alongside the ordinary laborers, he helps supply the raw metal needed for Edwin VanCleef's secret projects.",al={"why is miner johnson here","miner johnson deadmines why","what brought miner johnson here"},it="why_here",add="c0432457"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="For prospectors, Johnson shows the danger of mining beneath Westfall, where he guards mineral deposits with his pickaxe.",["faction:Alliance"]="Defeating Johnson disrupts the ore supply feeding the Defias war machine beneath Moonbrook."},kw={"alcove","deadmines","defias","elite","miner johnson","moonbrook","rare","shredder","westfall"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines"},src={"Miner Johnson"}}
E["npc:mr-smite"] = {t="npc",n="Mr. Smite",z="deadmines",s="At Ironclad Cove, Mr. Smite keeps watch over the Defias ship and its crew. The tauren serves Captain Greenskin as first mate, guarding the docks where Edwin VanCleef's dreadnaught is being fitted out. Any intruder who meets him faces a changing array of weapons and formidable strength.",h="At Ironclad Cove, Mr.",sec={{t="First Mate of the Cove",b="Mr. Smite keeps order on the docks of Ironclad Cove as first mate to the goblin Captain Greenskin. The Defias Brotherhood is made up mostly of disaffected humans and goblin tinkerers, yet Smite is a battle-hardened tauren far from Kalimdor's plains. He has charge of a rowdy pirate crew while they fit out Edwin VanCleef's secret dreadnaught, and he allows no disruption to the work.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Weaponmaster",b="Mr. Smite fights with more than brute force; he is a showman and a versatile weaponmaster. He toys with challengers, drawing out the fight and offering them a false hope of victory. When pressed, he stamps the ground with such force that foes are stunned, then searches a nearby chest for another weapon. He begins with a quick dueling blade, moves to twin cleaving reavers, and brings out a huge two-handed warhammer when pushed far enough.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a tauren working with human bandits in Westfall?",a="Most tauren live in Kalimdor with their Horde allies, but mercenary outcasts and wanderers sometimes travel east. Mr. Smite is Captain Greenskin's first mate, keeping the crew in line at Ironclad Cove as they ready the dreadnaught for sea.",al={"why tauren in deadmines","mr smite lore","tauren pirate"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Mr. Smite's superior?",a="Mr. Smite answers to Captain Greenskin, the goblin captain of the pirate vessel anchored in Ironclad Cove. Edwin VanCleef leads the Defias Brotherhood and stands above them in its wider conspiracy.",al={"who is smite's boss","who does mr smite work for"},it="ties"},{q="What weapons does Mr. Smite use during the fight?",a="Mr. Smite begins with a Thief's Blade, then retreats to his chest for a pair of Smite's Reavers. When pressed to his limits, he draws Smite's Mighty Hammer.",al={"smite weapons","what does smite pull out of the chest"},gp=true},{q="Where can Mr. Smite be found?",a="Mr. Smite watches the wooden piers of Ironclad Cove, the last cavern in the Deadmines. He guards the gangplank to the giant Defias dreadnaught.",al={"mr smite location","where is smite"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Mr. Smite fight alone?",a="Mr. Smite has two Defias rogues hidden nearby, ready to ambush trespassers advancing along the pier toward the ship.",al={"smite adds","smite bodyguards"},gp=true},{q="What makes Mr. Smite so dangerous in close quarters?",a="His tauren War Stomp sends shockwaves across the wooden dock and stuns the whole party, giving Mr. Smite time to rearm from his footlocker and return with heavier weapons.",al={"smite stun","smite war stomp"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Mr. Smite?",a="Mr. Smite is a formidable tauren weaponmaster serving as the first mate aboard the juggernaut hidden deep within the Deadmines. Working directly beneath Captain Greenskin, he commands the Defias Brotherhood's dock defenses and keeps their scoundrels in line with an iron fist and an arsenal of deadly weapons.",al={"who is smite","mr smite identity","what is mr smite"},it="identity",add="ecfcf591"},{q="Whose side is Mr. Smite on?",a="Despite being a tauren, Mr. Smite owes no allegiance to the Horde or his kin in Kalimdor. He is firmly aligned with Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood, serving as second-in-command to their goblin naval commander, Captain Greenskin.",al={"mr smite faction","who does smite work for","is smite horde or defias"},it="side",add="8cad5068"},{q="Why is Mr. Smite famous or feared?",a="Smite is feared for his sheer physical brutality and erratic combat mastery. He is notorious for toying with his victims, letting them believe they have gained the upper hand before stunning them with an earth-shattering stomp and drawing increasingly lethal weapons from his chest to finish them off.",al={"why is mr smite feared","mr smite reputation","why is smite famous"},it="fame",add="1c026e95"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For a traveler from Mulgore, seeing a tauren serve as first mate among seafaring outlaws in the Eastern Kingdoms is jarring.",["class:Warrior"]="Mr. Smite shows disciplined skill, moving from quick one-handed strikes to paired axes and punishing blows with a two-handed hammer.",["faction:Alliance"]="Mr. Smite blocks Alliance agents from reaching the gangplank and Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef beyond it."},kw={"captain greenskin","deadmines","first mate","ironclad cove","mr smite","mr. smite","smite's mighty hammer","smite's reaver","tauren pirate","thief's blade"},rel={"subzone:ironclad-cove","npc:captain-greenskin","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:tauren"},src={"Mr. Smite"}}
E["npc:rhahk-zor"] = {t="npc",n="Rhahk'Zor",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Rhahk'Zor drives the work forward by force. As head foreman, he keeps Defias laborers and miners in line while they build Edwin VanCleef's underground fortress.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Rhahk'Zor drives the work forward by force.",sec={{t="The Foreman of the Deep",b="The Defias Brotherhood has turned Moonbrook's abandoned gold mines into an underground fortress. Rhahk'Zor was appointed head foreman to coordinate the work. He oversees the excavation crews and laborers as they carve tunnels and build VanCleef's secret projects.",sp=0},{t="Brute Motivation",b="Rhahk'Zor keeps order with muscle and an immense stone-headed hammer. Defias diggers and goblin engineers know that defiance or falling behind schedule can bring a crushing blow from the towering foreman.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhahk'Zor?",a="Rhahk'Zor is an ogre and the Defias Brotherhood's foreman and enforcer in the Deadmines. He watches over the first excavation tunnels and keeps the workforce digging and in line.",al={"rhahkzor","who is the ogre boss in deadmines","deadmines first boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an ogre working for the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef's rebellion depends on the muscle and mercenary talent it can acquire. Rhahk'Zor's strength and intimidation make him a fit foreman for the grueling work of excavating the mines.",al={"why is there an ogre in deadmines","rhahkzor defias"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Rhahk'Zor's job in the mines?",a="Rhahk'Zor oversees construction in the mines. He supervises miners, goblins, and Defias builders as they hollow out caverns, maintain equipment, and build fortifications for the Brotherhood.",al={"what does rhahkzor do","rhahkzor role"},it="purpose"},{q="Where in the Deadmines is Rhahk'Zor located?",a="Rhahk'Zor is past the first miner tunnels, in the early quarry chambers. He stands in front of the first heavy door leading deeper into the mine.",al={"rhahkzor location","where is rhahkzor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Rhahk'Zor have any connection to the ogres from the First War?",a="Ogres lived in the Deadmines during the First War, before Blackhand's Horde wiped them out. Whether Rhahk'Zor belongs to those earlier clans or is a brute hired by VanCleef remains unconfirmed.",al={"first war ogres deadmines","ogre lore deadmines"},it="history"},{q="What happens when Rhahk'Zor is defeated?",a="Defeating Rhahk'Zor breaks the Defias hold on the outer quarry and clears the way through the reinforced blast door he guards. The route leads deeper into the clandestine shipyards and workshops.",al={"rhahkzor door","after rhahkzor"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Rhahk'Zor on?",a="Rhahk'Zor serves the Defias Brotherhood under Edwin VanCleef. Despite being an ogre among primarily human rogues and outlaws, he holds a position of authority as the head foreman overseeing the Brotherhood's subterranean excavation efforts and construction projects.",al={"who does rhahk'zor work for","rhahk'zor faction","rhahk'zor alliance"},it="side",add="77e4622d"},{q="Who is Rhahk'Zor tied to?",a="Rhahk'Zor answers directly to Edwin VanCleef, the mastermind behind the Defias Brotherhood. In turn, Rhahk'Zor commands the Defias miners, laborers, and guards stationed throughout the upper caverns of the Deadmines.",al={"rhahk'zor connections","who leads rhahk'zor","rhahk'zor edwin vancleef"},it="ties",add="ff75ed44"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers entering Moonbrook, Rhahk'Zor shows that the Defias Brotherhood has grown beyond petty highway banditry into a heavily fortified army.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, facing Rhahk'Zor tests your endurance on the front line against a massive ogre swinging a sledgehammer that shatters stone and bone.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you see Rhahk'Zor drive workers with crude brutality, turning Westfall's storied old gold mines into a rushed industrial war machine."},kw={"deadmines","defias","foreman","hammer","ogre","rhahk'zor","rhahkzor","vancleef"},rel={"zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","subzone:deadmines","quest:65","topic:first-war"},src={"Rhahk'Zor"}}
E["npc:shoni-the-shilent"] = {t="npc",n="Shoni the Shilent",z="deadmines",s="In Stormwind’s Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent sends a crew beneath Westfall. She leads the gnomish effort to reclaim Gnomeregan and seeks power for the machines meant to break a path back into the city.",h="In Stormwind’s Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent sends a crew beneath Westfall.",sec={{t="Commander of the Deep",b="Shoni the Shilent directs a gnomish assault crew from Stormwind’s Dwarven District. With Gnomeregan held by troggs, she plans to retake the city and sends operatives into the tunnels beneath Westfall for the parts her crew needs.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Reclamation",b="Shoni’s plan depends on the gnomes’ gyrodrillmatic excavationators, heavy machines built to break through Gnomeregan’s underground borders and open a way for an assault. The machines lack power, so she seeks the intact Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from a working goblin shredder deep in the Deadmines. She also sends adventurers into Gnomeregan to dismantle its robots for spare parts to repair her fleet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni the Shilent leads the Gnomeregan underground assault crew from Stormwind’s Dwarven District. She coordinates efforts to reclaim the city.",al={"who is shoni","shoni lore","shoni the shilent npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Shoni?",a="You can find Shoni among the anvils and workshops of Stormwind City’s Dwarven District, near the blacksmithing and engineering areas.",al={"where is shoni","shoni location","find shoni"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Shoni interested in the Deadmines?",a="A working goblin shredder lies deep in the Deadmines. Shoni seeks its intact Gnoam Sprecklesprocket to power the gyrodrillmatic excavationators and break through Gnomeregan’s underground borders.",al={"shoni deadmines","why send to deadmines","gyrodrillmatic quest"},it="wants"},{q="Why is she called 'the Shilent'?",a="No one knows the origin of Shoni’s epithet. She commands the Gnomeregan underground assault crew.",al={"shoni nickname","why shilent","silent gnome"},it="name"},{q="Whose side is Shoni the Shilent on?",a="Shoni is loyal to Gnomeregan and the Grand Alliance. Operating out of the Dwarven District in Stormwind City, she serves as the commander of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew, coordinating specialized technical efforts on behalf of her displaced people.",al={"shoni faction","who does shoni work for","shoni the shilent alliance"},it="side",add="3c03f847"},{q="Why is Shoni the Shilent here in Stormwind?",a="Following the fall of Gnomeregan, Shoni established herself among the tinkerers and craftsmen of Stormwind's Dwarven District. From here, she directs the underground assault team and gathers the necessary mechanical components and weaponry needed to support ongoing gnome operations.",al={"why is shoni in stormwind","what is shoni doing here","shoni purpose"},it="why_here",add="0ba3c461"},{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent tied to?",a="Shoni commands the Gnomeregan underground assault crew, maintaining deep ties to the gnomish military and engineering ranks. Stationed within Stormwind City, she works in close coordination with fellow Alliance engineers and soldiers seeking to reclaim their technological heritage.",al={"shoni affiliations","who does shoni command","shoni allies"},it="ties",add="076c3e36"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, helping Shoni brings your people closer to breaking back into Gnomeregan and reclaiming their fallen home.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the mechanical complexity of Shoni’s gyrodrillmatic excavationators, which she hopes to power with a shredder’s salvaged heart from beneath Moonbrook."},kw={"deadmines","dwarven district","excavationators","gnome","gyrodrillmatic","shilent","shoni","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","zone:deadmines","quest:2040","quest:2928","quest:2041","topic:gnome","zone:gnomeregan"},src={"Shoni the Shilent"}}
E["npc:sneed"] = {t="npc",n="Sneed",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Sneed directs the Defias Brotherhood’s timber work. From the Mast Room, he pilots a heavy shredder of his own design to cut lumber for Edwin VanCleef’s secret juggernaut.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Sneed directs the Defias Brotherhood’s timber work.",sec={{t="The Defias Lumbermaster",b="The Defias Brotherhood draws most of its members from human stonemasons and laborers, but an ironclad warship needs skilled trades. Edwin VanCleef brought Sneed in for his engineering knowledge and ruthless efficiency. Sneed works in the Mast Room, beside the underground rail network. There he directs the felling, cutting, and shaping of timber for VanCleef’s colossal dreadnaught.",sp=0},{t="Industrial Brutality",b="Sneed cares about cutting costs and meeting quotas, whatever the consequences. He directs the work from a custom shredder fitted with oversized buzz saws. Its blades turn raw trunks into shipbuilding timber in seconds. When intruders corner him, Sneed uses the machine’s armor to grind them down. If it fails, he scrambles from the wreckage and fights barehanded.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sneed?",a="Sneed is a goblin engineer and lumbermaster working for Edwin VanCleef. He oversees the timber work in the Deadmines for the Defias juggernaut.",al={"who is sneed","sneed lore","what is sneed"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Sneed be found?",a="Sneed works in the Mast Room, a lumber mill chamber along the mining tracks in the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook.",al={"sneed location","where is sneed","sneed room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is a goblin working for the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef needed specialized industrial knowledge and quick results for his secret warship. He hired mercenary goblins like Sneed, who care little for politics or ethics when the coin is good.",al={"why is sneed with defias","goblin in deadmines","why defias hire goblins"},it="motive"},{q="What is Sneed piloting in battle?",a="Sneed pilots Sneed’s Shredder, a heavy, saw-wielding bipedal machine he built to harvest and slice timber at great speed.",al={"sneed robot","sneed mech","sneed's shredder"},it="power"},{q="What happens when his shredder is destroyed?",a="Destroying the shredder does not end the fight. Sneed climbs from its wreckage and keeps fighting intruders on foot.",al={"sneed phase 2","sneed out of shredder","does sneed die with shredder"},gp=true},{q="What is Sneed building timber for?",a="Sneed’s timber travels downstream to Ironclad Cove, where the Brotherhood is assembling a massive warship to strike back at Stormwind.",al={"why sneed cutting wood","mast room purpose","deadmines wood"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Sneed on?",a="Sneed works squarely for Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood. While goblins are typically neutral merchants driven solely by profit, Sneed serves as VanCleef's dedicated lumbermaster. He oversees the Brotherhood's covert industrial logging deep within the Deadmines, throwing his engineering prowess and ruthless efficiency behind their campaign against Stormwind.",al={"sneed faction","who does sneed work for","is sneed defias"},it="side",add="a403ba53"},{q="What does Sneed want?",a="Sneed's goal is straightforward: build the Defias juggernaut as cheaply and swiftly as possible. Hired for his ruthless efficiency, he drives his logging operations around the clock, harvesting timber with his custom-built shredder to keep construction of the Brotherhood's secret warship moving without delay or costly waste.",al={"sneed goal","what is sneed trying to do","sneed motives"},it="wants",add="9b5b74a3"},{q="Why is Sneed here in the Deadmines?",a="Sneed is stationed in the Mast Room of the Deadmines to supply the heavy timber required for the Defias Brotherhood's massive naval vessel. Operating from the subterranean logging yard, he pilots his shredder to clear, mill, and prepare the massive wooden beams that will form the backbone of the juggernaut.",al={"why is sneed in deadmines","sneed purpose deadmines","why is sneed in the mast room"},it="why_here",add="e888ebfc"},{q="Who is Sneed tied to?",a="Sneed reports directly to Edwin VanCleef, the grand leader of the Defias Brotherhood. VanCleef contracted the goblin engineer to supervise lumber operations within the cavern system, integrating Sneed and his machinery into the broader Defias command hierarchy alongside figures like Rhahk'Zor and Gilnid.",al={"who does sneed report to","sneed edwin vancleef","sneed defias ties"},it="ties",add="5de8a7f0"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Sneed’s custom shredder shows goblin craftsmanship at work: efficient, heavily armed, and pushed beyond standard safety limits for speed.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Sneed’s machine as goblin ingenuity: loud, hazardous, and built without regard for comfort or lasting structure.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can cripple the Defias Brotherhood’s shipbuilding efforts by stopping Sneed’s timber supply to Ironclad Cove."},kw={"deadmines","edwin vancleef","goblin","juggernaut","lumbermaster","mast room","shredder","sneed","sneed's shredder"},rel={"npc:sneed-s-shredder","subzone:mast-room","zone:deadmines","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:goblin"},src={"Sneed"}}
E["npc:sneed-s-shredder"] = {t="npc",n="Sneed's Shredder",z="deadmines",s="Deep in the Deadmines, Sneed's Shredder cuts timber and guards the works. Goblin taskmaster Sneed pilots the machine for Edwin VanCleef's shipwrights, turning its blades against intruders.",h="Deep in the Deadmines, Sneed's Shredder cuts timber and guards the works.",sec={{t="Industrial Terror",b="In the Deadmines foundry, goblin shredders cut timber for Edwin VanCleef's hidden juggernaut. They also meet intruders with armored force. Sneed oversees the lumber works and pilots this modified machine himself, wielding its oversized buzzsaw as a weapon of defense.",sp=0},{t="A Deadly Cockpit",b="Sneed rides above the spinning blades in an open cockpit, protected by heavy iron plating. The machine's clatter can scatter his foes. When the shredder breaks down and collapses in sparks, Sneed leaps from the wreckage and fights on.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Sneed's Shredder used for in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood uses goblin machinery to cut through stone and process timber for its secret juggernaut. Sneed's Shredder mills wood and enforces order in the underground works.",al={"why is there a shredder in deadmines","shredder purpose deadmines"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens when the shredder is destroyed?",a="When the shredder breaks down, Sneed survives. The goblin pilot emerges from the wreckage with his own weapons and attacks intruders fiercely.",al={"does sneed die with the shredder","sneed shredder phase 2"}},{q="Why do the Defias Brotherhood have goblin technology?",a="Edwin VanCleef hired goblin engineers, craftsmen, and mercenary laborers to run mechanical works beneath Westfall, including steam powered forges, gun foundries, and woodmills.",al={"defias goblins","why are goblins in deadmines"},it="ties"},{q="Can the shredder be hacked or controlled by engineers?",a="A Gnomish Universal Remote can briefly override the shredder's controls and wrest command from Sneed.",al={"control sneed shredder","gnomish universal remote sneed"},gp=true},{q="Does Sneed's Shredder carry anything valuable?",a="Yes. The intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, is sought by Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind. She needs it to power the gnomes' gyrodrillmatic excavationators for an assault on Gnomeregan.",al={"sneed shredder quest item","what drops from sneed shredder"},gp=true},{q="Who pilots the shredder?",a="Sneed, a goblin supervisor, pilots the machine and directs logging and carpentry deep in the Deadmines.",al={"who drives sneed shredder","sneed pilot"},it="identity"},{q="Whose side is Sneed's Shredder on?",a="The mechanical beast fights under the banner of the Defias Brotherhood. While goblin engineers frequently work as neutral mercenaries for whoever pays best, Sneed and his armored timber-cutter are firmly committed to Edwin VanCleef's operation deep beneath Moonbrook.",al={"sneed shredder faction","who does sneed serve","is sneeds shredder defias"},it="side",add="a3f5b00d"},{q="What does Sneed want with his shredder?",a="Piloting a walking lumber mill bristling with spinning saw blades, Sneed is bent on reducing any intruders into fine planks of wood. Beyond processing timber and defending the subterranean works, he wants little more than to turn you into fresh sawdust for disturbing the Defias compound.",al={"sneed goals","what does sneed want","sneeds shredder purpose"},it="wants",add="b57110af"},{q="Why is Sneed's Shredder in the Deadmines?",a="Constructing an underground empire requires tremendous engineering support, lumber, and heavy defense. Sneed's Shredder is stationed in the lumber-filled caverns of the Deadmines to harvest timber for the Brotherhood's secret projects and to grind any trespassing Alliance agents into mulch.",al={"why is sneeds shredder here","why is sneed in deadmines","shredder location deadmines"},it="why_here",add="faf23f8c"},{q="Why is Sneed's Shredder so feared?",a="Beyond its massive whirring sawblades, the mechanized terror strikes raw panic into the hearts of invaders. Sneed routinely unleashes frightful bursts of clattering noise and shrieking metal that terrify adventurers, sending them fleeing straight into the arms of waiting Defias goblins.",al={"why is sneeds shredder scary","sneeds shredder reputation","terrify sneeds shredder"},it="fame",add="0d282aa3"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can briefly override the shredder with a Gnomish Universal Remote.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know Shoni the Shilent wants the goblin built machine's power supply to drive drills for an assault on Gnomeregan.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can cripple the lumber works supporting Edwin VanCleef's secret war fleet by defeating Sneed and his machine."},kw={"buzzsaw","deadmines","defias","goblin","lumber","remote","shredder","sneed","vancleef"},rel={"npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","quest:2040","topic:goblin"},src={"Sneed's Shredder"}}
E["npc:wilder-thistlenettle"] = {t="npc",n="Wilder Thistlenettle",z="deadmines",s="In Stormwind’s Dwarven District, Wilder Thistlenettle drinks alone with old grief. He once entered Moonbrook’s Deadmines with his brother and their mining crew, but a cave-in left him the sole survivor.",h="In Stormwind’s Dwarven District, Wilder Thistlenettle drinks alone with old grief.",sec={{t="A Bitter Survivor",b="Wilder Thistlenettle drinks away his sorrow in an alehouse near the Dwarven District’s southeastern gates. Years ago, he joined his brother and their companions in the deep lodes of Moonbrook’s Deadmines. A cave-in sealed the rest of the crew underground, and Wilder barely reached the surface alive.",sp=0},{t="Ghosts of the Deep",b="Wilder’s brother and the lost mining company haunt the Deadmines as restless undead. Dark magic or unfinished business keeps them bound to the subterranean ruins. Grief and guilt weigh on Wilder, who asks travelers bound for the mines to recover mementos of the fallen and bring his brother peace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder sits inside a quiet pub in Stormwind City’s Dwarven District, just inside the right side of its southeastern entrance.",al={"wilder thistlenettle location","where is wilder","thistlenettle stormwind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to his brother in the Deadmines?",a="A sudden tunnel collapse trapped Wilder’s brother with the other miners. Wilder escaped and seeks news of those left below.",al={"wilder brother deadmines","what happened to brother","thistlenettle brother lore"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Wilder need adventurers?",a="Wilder asks travelers entering the Deadmines to recover personal mining union badges from the lost workers and investigate what happened to his brother.",al={"wilder quests","what does wilder want","collecting memories quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner currently drinking his sorrows away in Stormwind City's Dwarven District. He was part of a mining expedition into the Deadmines alongside his brother, but tragedy struck deep beneath the earth.",al={"who is wilder","wilder thistlenettle lore","about wilder thistlenettle"},it="identity",add="2e3a3cea"},{q="Whose side is Wilder Thistlenettle on?",a="Wilder is loyal to the Alliance and his dwarven kin. He spends his days brooding in an empty tavern in Stormwind, seeking aid from trusted Alliance adventurers brave enough to enter the Deadmines.",al={"wilder thistlenettle faction","who does wilder work for","is wilder alliance"},it="side",add="cb45d77d"},{q="Why is Wilder Thistlenettle here in Stormwind?",a="After narrowly escaping a catastrophic cave-in inside the Deadmines that claimed his brother and crew, Wilder fled back to the safety of Stormwind City. Traumatized and grief-stricken, he took refuge in a quiet tavern in the Dwarven District.",al={"why is wilder in stormwind","why is wilder here","wilder dwarven district why"},it="why_here",add="cf83a843"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Wilder’s grief recalls the dangers of deep delving and the duty to honor fallen guild brothers.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know unstable earth can entomb even seasoned crews deep underground."},kw={"brother","cave-in","deadmines","dwarven district","miner","stormwind","thistlenettle","wilder"},rel={"quest:167","quest:168","subzone:dwarven-district","zone:stormwind","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","topic:dwarf","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Wilder Thistlenettle"}}
E["quest:166"] = {t="quest",n="The Defias Brotherhood",z="deadmines",s="In Westfall, The Defias Brotherhood still holds the farmlands in fear. Gryan Stoutmantle has found their stronghold beneath Moonbrook and calls for a final blow against their leader.",h="In Westfall, The Defias Brotherhood still holds the farmlands in fear.",sec={{t="A Sentence Passed",b="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia have fought the Defias Brotherhood across Westfall for months. Now the thieves' stronghold lies exposed beneath Moonbrook. Stoutmantle orders Edwin VanCleef assassinated, believing his death will break the rebellion once and for all.",sp=0},{t="Into the Labyrinth",b="You face winding shafts deep beneath the Deadmines, where renegade stonemasons, goblin engineers, and heavy iron blast doors guard the way. At the central dry dock, VanCleef oversees the final construction of his grand war vessel. His death would sever the command that holds the outlaw network together.",sp=1},{t="Shadows of a Greater Conspiracy",b="Gryan Stoutmantle believes VanCleef's death will begin the end for the Brotherhood. Yet an unsent letter rests on the fallen guildmaster's body. It hints that Westfall's uprising was tied to a wider web reaching into Stormwind City's nobility.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the goal of this quest?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle asks you to enter the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook, kill Edwin VanCleef, and bring his severed head to Sentinel Hill.",al={"quest objective","what do i do","what is this quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef once served as Grand Mason of the Stonemasons Guild and led Stormwind City's rebuilding after the orcs razed it in the First War. After a bitter dispute with the House of Nobles over payment, he founded the Defias Brotherhood to seek vengeance on the kingdom.",al={"who is vancleef","vancleef identity","edwin vancleef lore"},it="target"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle order an assassination?",a="The People's Militia lacks the regular army reinforcements from Stormwind needed for a long war. Stoutmantle sees the removal of the Brotherhood's leadership as Westfall's only realistic chance to break the syndicate's grip on the farmlands.",al={"why kill vancleef","stoutmantle motive","why death penalty"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Edwin VanCleef be found?",a="Edwin VanCleef is hidden deep in the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook. Gryan Stoutmantle asks you to enter the hideout and find him.",al={"vancleef location","where is edwin vancleef","deadmines boss location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does killing VanCleef destroy the Defias completely?",a="Stoutmantle hopes VanCleef's death will break the Brotherhood's hold on Westfall. The outcome and any further discoveries await the assault.",al={"is defias defeated","are defias gone","end of brotherhood"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What item of note is found on VanCleef upon his defeat?",a="Stoutmantle demands VanCleef's head as proof. Other discoveries inside the hideout come during the assault.",al={"vancleef drop","unsent letter","what does vancleef drop"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of VanCleef for?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle demands undeniable proof that Edwin VanCleef is truly dead. The Defias Brotherhood has terrorized Westfall from the shadows for years, spreading rumors and evading capture. Presenting VanCleef's severed head brings undeniable closure to the People's Militia and signals to the embattled farmers that their greatest tormentor has finally fallen.",al={"why take vancleefs head","head of vancleef purpose","why do i need vancleef head"},it="item",add="e9d4d384"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle send you instead of the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is stretched to its limit simply defending Sentinel Hill and Westfall's scattered homesteads from daily bandit raids and gnoll incursions. Stormwind has refused to send reinforcements, leaving Stoutmantle without the disciplined, heavy strike force needed to breach the fortified depths of the Deadmines. He must rely on seasoned, capable adventurers like you to strike directly at the heart of the conspiracy.",al={"why doesn't the militia attack deadmines","why send me against vancleef","why doesn't stoutmantle kill vancleef"},it="why_me",add="48642626"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you face a bitter tragedy in VanCleef's death: the artisan who rebuilt your capital from ashes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you strike an early blow to secure Westfall's breadbasket while Stormwind's throne cannot spare its own troops.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you face VanCleef, a famed rogue and master artisan, in his inner sanctum. The clash tests the training of any stealth operative."},kw={"deadmines","head","juggernaut","militia","moonbrook","stonemasons","stoutmantle","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:edwin-vancleef","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","zone:deadmines","topic:defias-brotherhood","zone:westfall","quest:12","quest:65","topic:alliance"},m={start="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=166,ri={"Head of VanCleef"}},src={"The Defias Brotherhood (7)"}}
E["quest:167"] = {t="quest",n="Oh Brother. . .",z="deadmines",s="Wilder Thistlenettle waits in Stormwind after a cave-in beneath Moonbrook. He asks you to search the mines for his brother, Foreman Thistlenettle, or recover the dwarf's Explorers' League Badge.",h="Wilder Thistlenettle waits in Stormwind after a cave-in beneath Moonbrook.",sec={{t="A Trapped Expedition",b="Wilder Thistlenettle and his brother worked for a mining company in the tunnels beneath Moonbrook. Thieves swarmed the mines, then a cave-in sealed the lower passages. Wilder escaped to Stormwind, but his brother and the rest of the crew remained trapped behind the rubble.",sp=0},{t="The Grim Fate of Foreman Thistlenettle",b="Foreman Thistlenettle did not survive being trapped beneath the rubble. Dark energies in the abandoned mines raised the dwarf as an undead husk. He wanders the tunnels with other restless corpses, carrying his Explorers' League Badge, the last token of who he was.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I start the quest \"Oh Brother. . .\"?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle offers the search in Stormwind City's Dwarven District.",al={"quest giver oh brother","who gives oh brother","where to get oh brother"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Where is Foreman Thistlenettle located?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle wanders the outer mine corridors beneath Moonbrook in Westfall, somewhere along the tunnels leading to the portal.",al={"foreman thistlenettle location","where is thistlenettle","where is the brother"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happened to Foreman Thistlenettle?",a="A cave-in trapped Foreman Thistlenettle and his mining party in the caverns, and no word has come from them since. Wilder needs to find his brother or at least his badge to learn what happened.",al={"is thistlenettle alive","what happened to the brother","thistlenettle lore"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What item do I need to retrieve?",a="You need Foreman Thistlenettle's Explorers' League Badge, which he always carried. Find him deep in the Deadmines tunnels, and the badge will be with him.",al={"oh brother quest item","what drops for oh brother"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What was the expedition doing in Moonbrook?",a="The Thistlenettle brothers worked for a mining company beneath Moonbrook before Defias bandits ambushed them and a sudden collapse separated them.",al={"why were the dwarves in westfall","explorers league deadmines","why were they in moonbrook"},it="history"},{q="Is this quest completed inside the Deadmines dungeon instance?",a="No. You can find Foreman Thistlenettle in the contested mine tunnels leading to the portal, without entering the dungeon. He is an elite foe.",al={"is oh brother inside deadmines instance","do i need a dungeon group"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle want this done?",a="Wilder barely escaped with his life when the tunnels collapsed deep beneath Moonbrook. His brother and the rest of the mining expedition never emerged, swallowed by the dark and the thieves infesting the passages. Left in agonizing uncertainty back in Stormwind, Wilder seeks peace of mind. He needs to know whether his brother yet lives or if he met a grim fate in the deep.",al={"why does wilder want his brother found","wilder thistlenettle motive","why find foreman thistlenettle"},it="motive",add="7bf03114"},{q="What is Thistlenettle's Badge?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle carried an Explorers' League Badge marking his standing with Ironforge's guild of diggers and adventurers. Should you find no living dwarf in the depths, recovering this personal token serves as proof of his fate, granting his grieving brother final closure.",al={"what is thistlenettles badge","thistlenettle explorers league badge","why get the badge"},it="item",add="ebc7a172"},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle ask you instead of going himself?",a="Wilder barely made it out alive when disaster struck. The sprawling labyrinth beneath Moonbrook is crawling with cutthroats and dangerous hazards, far beyond what an escaped miner can brave alone. Seeing a capable adventurer, he places his hopes on you to succeed where he could only flee.",al={"why doesnt wilder go himself","why send me deadmines","why does wilder need help"},it="why_me",add="5e05fe78"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, the loss of an Explorers' League foreman in human lands touches on brotherhood, stonecutting, and the League's tireless work.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how the Defias and horrors beneath the ground have harmed innocent people near Stormwind."},kw={"badge","deadmines","explorers' league","moonbrook","stormwind","thistlenettle","undead","westfall","wilder"},rel={"npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","zone:westfall","topic:explorers-league","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wilder Thistlenettle",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=167,ri={"Thistlenettle's Badge"}},src={"Oh Brother. . ."}}
E["quest:168"] = {t="quest",n="Collecting Memories",z="deadmines",s="In Stormwind City, Wilder Thistlenettle asks you to remember the miners lost beneath Moonbrook. He wants their Miners' Union Cards returned to their grieving families.",h="In Stormwind City, Wilder Thistlenettle asks you to remember the miners lost beneath Moonbrook.",sec={{t="A Tragic Collapse",b="Before lawlessness and the Defias Brotherhood took hold in Moonbrook, Westfall's mines supported many working-class families. Wilder Thistlenettle survived a cave-in that buried one wing of the tunnels. Many of his friends and fellow miners died underground, beyond the reach of rescue. Their families in Stormwind never learned for certain what had become of them.",sp=0},{t="Restless Remains",b="The miners who died in the collapse now wander the tunnels outside the main iron works as undead. You search those haunted passages for the Miners' Union Cards, facing the remains of the men Wilder worked beside. Bringing the cards back to Stormwind will tell their families what happened and let Wilder honor his fallen companions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wilder Thistlenettle?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle is a dwarven miner in Stormwind City. He survived a cave-in beneath Westfall that killed his close coworkers, and seeks to bring confirmation and peace to their families.",al={"wilder thistlenettle","quest giver","who gives collecting memories"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the miners in the Deadmines?",a="A cave-in trapped and killed a crew of miners in a wing of the Moonbrook dig sites. Their bodies and spirits now haunt the abandoned passages as undead.",al={"why are there undead miners","mine collapse","deadmines cave in"},it="history"},{q="Why does Wilder want their Miners' Union Cards?",a="The Miners' Union Cards identify the workers who died in the collapse. Since their bodies were never recovered, Wilder wants to return the cards so their families in Stormwind can learn what happened.",al={"what are the union cards for","miners union cards"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the union cards found?",a="The cards lie in the haunted outer tunnels beneath Moonbrook, in the corridors before the secured entrance to the Deadmines proper.",al={"where do i find the cards","undead deadmines location","where are the dead miners"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Did the Defias Brotherhood cause the cave-in?",a="Wilder remembers a terrible mining accident and cave-in. The Defias Brotherhood now rules the deep passages, but the collapse appears to have been an industrial accident that trapped the miners.",al={"did defias cause the cave in","who collapsed the mine"},it="conflict"},{q="Are the miners considered part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. They were ordinary union laborers when the cave-in struck. Their undead remains wander the cavern edges, apart from Edwin VanCleef's organized Defias forces deeper inside.",al={"are dead miners defias","are undead miners with defias"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Miners' Union Card?",a="These union cards served as official identification for the laborers working the rich veins of the Moonbrook mines before the catastrophe. Now, they are the only lasting proof of who perished beneath the earth when the tunnels collapsed. Recovering them is the sole way to confirm which specific workers met their end in the depths, allowing Wilder Thistlenettle to notify their grieving families in Stormwind and offer them closure.",al={"miners union card","what are the union cards","union card"},it="item",add="e1328ead"},{q="Why does Wilder Thistlenettle need an adventurer for this task?",a="Wilder Thistlenettle survived the terrible collapse, but the depths of the Moonbrook mines have since fallen into perilous chaos. The area surrounding the old cave-in is overrun with hostile forces and restless dead, far beyond what an ordinary civilian or former miner can face. Without official city guards dispatched into the treacherous ruins of Westfall, Wilder relies on capable adventurers who already intend to delve into the mines to search the wreckage for his lost friends.",al={"why me collecting memories","why does wilder need help","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="22601dce"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know the dread of a shaft collapse. Recovering the lost union cards gives that fear a solemn weight.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know the bonds forged underground and the honor owed to fallen kin. Wilder Thistlenettle's plea reaches close to home.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help the grieving families of Westfall workers who endure hard times within Stormwind's walls."},kw={"collecting memories","deadmines","miners union card","moonbrook","stormwind","undead miners","wilder thistlenettle"},rel={"npc:wilder-thistlenettle","zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:moonbrook","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wilder Thistlenettle",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=168,ri={"Miners' Union Card"}},src={"Collecting Memories"}}
E["quest:2040"] = {t="quest",n="Underground Assault",z="deadmines",s="Shoni the Shilent sends Alliance adventurers into the Deadmines for a power core. The displaced gnomes need it to power drills that can break through the rock around Gnomeregan and help reclaim their home.",h="Shoni the Shilent sends Alliance adventurers into the Deadmines for a power core.",sec={{t="A Desperate Ingenuity",b="After Gnomeregan fell catastrophically to primitive troggs, surviving gnomish tinkerers fled across Khaz Modan and Stormwind. Shoni the Shilent is among the engineers already planning how to breach the rock around their lost home. Her gyrodrillmatic excavationators need great power to bore through the underground stone. Without local power grids in human lands, the gnomes have turned to goblin heavy machinery in the criminal underworld.",sp=0},{t="Looting the Defias Foundries",b="Deep in the twisting shafts of the Deadmines in Westfall, Edwin VanCleef's Defias Brotherhood employs goblin engineers to build war machines. One is a working goblin shredder, a lumbering automaton. Shoni sends Alliance operatives to destroy or dismantle it and recover its specialized heart, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket. The exiled gnomes need the goblin power supply to drive their drills through the underground rock and begin their counteroffensive to reclaim Gnomeregan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Underground Assault quest?",a="Shoni the Shilent, a gnomish engineer in Stormwind City's Dwarven District, gives it. Other gnomes often direct adventurers to her after mentioning her ambitious plans.",al={"quest giver underground assault","who gives underground assault","shoni quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="You recover the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket from a working goblin shredder deep in the Deadmines foundry tunnels in Westfall.",al={"sprecklesprocket location","where is sprecklesprocket","shredder part deadmines"},gp=true},{q="Why does Shoni need parts from a goblin shredder?",a="Gnomish gyrodrillmatic excavationators need immense portable power to breach the reinforced underground borders around Gnomeregan. The heavy-duty core running the Defias goblin shredder provides the exact mechanical output the drills require.",al={"why goblin parts","why shredder power supply","sprecklesprocket purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What is the broader goal of this mission?",a="The exiled gnomes plan to power heavy excavation drills, tunnel through the rocky perimeter of captured Gnomeregan, and launch a surprise assault against the troggs occupying it.",al={"why do underground assault","reclaiming gnomeregan quest","gnome assault plan"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to Gnomeregan that caused this assault to be planned?",a="A subterranean trogg invasion rose from deep beneath Gnomeregan and overwhelmed the city. Toxic radiation contaminated it during the chaotic defense, forcing survivors to flee as refugees to Ironforge and Stormwind.",al={"why did gnomeregan fall","what happened to gnomeregan","trogg invasion"},it="history"},{q="Are the Defias Brotherhood and the troggs allied?",a="No, the Defias Brotherhood and the troggs have no connection. The Defias hired goblin tinkerers to build war machines in Westfall, and Shoni exploits their Deadmines foundry as a convenient source of high-yield goblin technology.",al={"defias and troggs","are troggs with defias"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket?",a="The Gnoam Sprecklesprocket is an intact, highly efficient goblin power supply housed within the shredder operating deep inside the Deadmines. Shoni the Shilent intends to integrate this power core directly into gnomish gyrodrillmatic excavationators. These heavy drilling machines need immense energy to bore through the dense, rocky underground perimeter shielding Gnomeregan, carving an entryway for the gnomish assault forces waiting to reclaim their home.",al={"what is gnoam sprecklesprocket","sprecklesprocket purpose","what does the shredder power supply do"},it="item",add="41842bc5"},{q="Why does Shoni send you after the goblin shredder in the Deadmines?",a="The Defias Brotherhood employs advanced goblin engineering, including a fully functional timber and mining shredder, to excavate and construct their secret operations beneath Moonbrook. Because these war machines utilize remarkably potent power cores, Shoni identified this machine as a prime salvage target. You are sent to dismantle or destroy the shredder deep inside the compound and extract its intact power unit before the Brotherhood puts it to further use.",al={"who is the target in deadmines","why kill the shredder","why is there a shredder in deadmines"},it="target",add="37ad24fa"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As an exiled gnomish adventurer, you help salvage a power core that can drive drills through the rocky walls of your fallen home and help drive the troggs from Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the audacious work of cannibalizing a brutal goblin shredder's power core to fuel precise gnomish excavation machinery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you strengthen Stormwind's bond with its displaced gnomish allies and strike at the Defias supply line."},kw={"deadmines","gnoam sprecklesprocket","gnomeregan","goblin shredder","gyrodrillmatic","shoni the shilent","troggs","underground assault"},rel={"npc:shoni-the-shilent","quest:2041","zone:deadmines","zone:gnomeregan","topic:goblin","topic:trogg","quest:2928"},m={start="Shoni the Shilent",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2040,ri={"Gnoam Sprecklesprocket"}},src={"Underground Assault"}}
E["quest:214"] = {t="quest",n="Red Silk Bandanas",z="deadmines",s="Scout Riell sends the People's Militia after Red Silk Bandanas in the Deadmines. Their fine weave marks the Defias leaders who direct the uprising in Westfall.",h="Scout Riell sends the People's Militia after Red Silk Bandanas in the Deadmines.",sec={{t="A Hierarchy in Cloth",b="Scout Riell and the People's Militia have learned that cloth marks rank in the Defias Brotherhood. Common cutpurses and highwaymen across Westfall tie coarse red cloth over their faces. Senior conspirators and inner-circle operatives wear fine red silk. Bringing back their bandanas strikes at the experienced officers coordinating Edwin VanCleef's uprising.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Core",b="The senior outlaws gather deep in the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook. Sentinels and scouts outside Sentinel Hill depend on freelance champions to enter the contested tunnels. Each silk bandana recovered means one fewer lieutenant organizing ambushes, guarding weapon caches, or enforcing VanCleef's rule across Westfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the Defias wear red bandanas?",a="The Defias wear red bandanas to hide their faces and show allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's rebellion. The red cloth marks their Brotherhood across Stormwind's territories.",al={"defias mask meaning","why red masks","defias uniform"},it="item"},{q="What makes the red silk bandanas special compared to regular bandanas?",a="Scout Riell says the fabric marks rank in the Brotherhood. Common street thugs wear coarse, cheap cloth, while veterans, officers, and trusted lieutenants wear red silk.",al={"why red silk","silk vs cloth defias","silk bandana difference"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Scout Riell?",a="Scout Riell serves the People's Militia in Westfall. The operative tracks Defias movements and directs adventurers against their strongholds around the Deadmines.",al={"scout riell westfall","who gives red silk bandanas quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the Defias wearing silk bandanas located?",a="Defias wearing silk bandanas gather in and around the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook. Edwin VanCleef's senior forces oversee underground operations there.",al={"where to find silk bandanas","deadmines silk bandana location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the People's Militia?",a="The People's Militia is a volunteer defense force formed by Gryan Stoutmantle and Westfall's embattled farmers. They protect their lands after the Stormwind army failed to provide enough garrisons.",al={"who are the people's militia","peoples militia westfall"},it="allies"},{q="Do these bandanas have any use outside of proving a kill?",a="For the People's Militia, the bandanas prove that high-ranking outlaws have been eliminated. Each one weakens the Brotherhood's command structure.",al={"can you wear red silk bandana","what are the bandanas for"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does Scout Riell want Defias bandanas collected?",a="Scout Riell is seeking to strike a decisive blow against the leadership of the Defias Brotherhood on behalf of the People's Militia. The militia knows that silk bandanas denote high-ranking officers rather than mere thugs. By eliminating these key figures and demanding their bandanas as proof, Riell hopes to shatter the brotherhood's command structure and finally reclaim Westfall for its people.",al={"why scout riell bandanas","scout riell motive","why collect red silk bandanas"},it="motive",add="09c03d28"},{q="Who are you being sent against?",a="You are hunting the elite officers and veterans of the Defias Brotherhood stationed in and around Edwin VanCleef's stronghold within the Deadmines. Unlike the rough cutthroats roaming Westfall's farmsteads, these high-ranking members guard the brotherhood's base of operations, oversee the hidden works deep beneath Moonbrook, and direct the syndicate's operations across the region.",al={"who are we hunting","red silk bandana target","who drops silk bandanas"},it="target",add="762e9a74"},{q="Why does Scout Riell ask you instead of the Stormwind guards?",a="Stormwind has virtually abandoned Westfall, offering little to no military support while the House of Nobles ignores the growing crisis. The local People's Militia is stretched thin, lacking the numbers, training, and resources to mount a frontal assault against fortified criminal bastions. Riell and her fellow scouts must rely on capable adventurers to infiltrate the treacherous Deadmines and confront the brotherhood's leadership directly.",al={"why not stormwind army","why send an adventurer","why need me"},it="why_me",add="966e78fe"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of the Alliance, every officer felled in the Deadmines loosens the Brotherhood's hold on Stormwind's breadbasket.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you know red silk marks veteran cutthroats and covert conspirators in the Defias tradition of underworld tradecraft.",["profession:Tailoring"]="As a tailor, you know fine red silk costs too much for common bandits. Its use shows how lavishly equipped and funded the Brotherhood's leadership is."},kw={"deadmines","defias brotherhood","moonbrook","peoples militia","red silk bandanas","scout riell","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"npc:scout-riell","zone:deadmines","quest:12","subzone:deadmines"},m={start="Scout Riell",level="17",faction="Alliance",id=214},src={"Red Silk Bandanas"}}
E["subzone:goblin-foundry"] = {t="subzone",n="Goblin Foundry",z="deadmines",s="In the Deadmines, goblins keep the Goblin Foundry working for the Defias Brotherhood. Gilnid oversees craftsmen and engineers around a great smelting cauldron.",h="In the Deadmines, goblins keep the Goblin Foundry working for the Defias Brotherhood.",sec={{t="Industrial Ambitions",b="Deep beneath Moonbrook, goblin craftsmen and engineers work at the Goblin Foundry for the Defias Brotherhood. Smelters and iron ramps fill the chamber as they make anchors and cannonballs.",sp=0},{t="Gilnid's Workshop",b="Gilnid oversees the goblin workforce at the foundry. Craftsmen keep production moving, while engineers use remote-controlled golems to defend the workshop. Narrow ramps and molten metal make the chamber dangerous for intruders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was being built in the Goblin Foundry?",a="Goblin craftsmen make heavy metalwork for the Defias Brotherhood, including anchors and cannonballs.",al={"what are they making here","foundry purpose","deadmines factory"},it="purpose"},{q="Why are there golems in the foundry?",a="Goblin engineers use remote-controlled golems to defend their workshop from intruders.",al={"why golems here","foundry robots","mechanical enemies deadmines"},it="threat"},{q="Where are the goblins who ran this workshop?",a="The goblin craftsmen and engineers are still at work in the foundry under Gilnid, the smelter.",al={"where are the goblins","foundry engineers","gilnid workers"},it="residents"},{q="What is the large structure in the center of the room?",a="A massive industrial smelting cauldron dominates the room's center. It melts ore hauled from the mines to forge armor plates and mechanical chassis.",al={"foundry center pot","smelting vat","cauldron in deadmines"}},{q="What is the Goblin Foundry?",a="The Goblin Foundry is a cavernous industrial workshop nestled deep within the Deadmines subterranean complex. Built and operated by mercenary goblin engineers contracted to the Defias Brotherhood, the facility houses massive smelting equipment, catwalks, and workshops intended to forge metalworks, tools, and mechanized implements of war for Edwin VanCleef's hidden rebellion.",al={"what is goblin foundry","goblin foundry lore","what is this foundry"},it="place",add="a84744f8"},{q="What happened at the Goblin Foundry?",a="Goblin craftsmen and engineers established the foundry as an active Defias workshop. Gilnid directs their metalworking, while engineers employ remote-controlled golems to defend it.",al={"what happened here","foundry history","goblin foundry story"},it="history",add="bbcfa33c"},{q="What work is done at the Goblin Foundry?",a="The foundry remains active. Goblin craftsmen and engineers work there under Gilnid, producing metalwork for the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"what work is done at goblin foundry","what do goblins make at the foundry","goblin foundry production"},it="purpose",add="60ac21cc"},{q="Is the Goblin Foundry dangerous?",a="The foundry is dangerous to intruders. Goblin craftsmen, engineers, and their remote-controlled golems defend narrow ramps around a massive smelting cauldron.",al={"is goblin foundry dangerous","foundry dangers","goblin foundry threat"},it="danger",add="22e4861d"},{q="Why is it called the Goblin Foundry?",a="The chamber is named after the goblin tinkerers and metallurgists hired by the Defias Brotherhood to run it. It was tailored specifically for goblin engineering and smelting, complete with elaborate ramps, blast cauldrons, and workbenches designed around their explosive industrial ambitions.",al={"why is it called goblin foundry","goblin foundry name origin","who named goblin foundry"},it="name",add="11526e87"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The foundry shows goblin metalworking and mechanical skill. Its engineers use remote-controlled golems to defend the workshop.",["faction:Alliance"]="Beneath Westfall, the Defias workshop reveals the scale of the Brotherhood's industrial resources."},kw={"cauldron","deadmines","defias","goblin foundry","vancleef"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","subzone:cauldron","topic:goblin"},src={"Goblin Foundry"}}
E["subzone:ironclad-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironclad Cove",z="deadmines",s="Deep beneath Westfall, Ironclad Cove holds a hidden shipyard and dock. The Defias Brotherhood builds its war juggernaught here, with a passage to the sea.",h="Deep beneath Westfall, Ironclad Cove holds a hidden shipyard and dock.",sec={{t="The Hidden Shipyard",b="Ironclad Cove lies at the deepest point of the Deadmines, where a vast sea cavern has become a fortified dockyard. Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood have built an enormous warship here, the juggernaught. Wooden scaffolding, islets, and loading catwalks fill the cavern, watched by Defias pirates, deckhands, and overseers. VanCleef aims to do more than raid Westfall's farmsteads: he plans to assemble a private naval force capable of bombarding Stormwind's shores.",sp=0},{t="Gateway to the Ocean",b="Colossal iron-reinforced sea doors fill the cavern wall. Beyond them lies the Great Sea, along the coast of northern Stranglethorn Vale. Hidden from Stormwind's naval fleet, the cove gives the Brotherhood an unmonitored route to move contraband, stage maritime raids, and prepare its naval assault.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the ship in Ironclad Cove being built for?",a="The juggernaught is the centerpiece of Edwin VanCleef's military ambitions. The Defias Brotherhood built the massive warship deep beneath the earth so it could pass unseen through subterranean water channels and strike Stormwind from the sea.",al={"why is there a ship here","what is the juggernaught","deadmines ship purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the large metal door in the cove lead?",a="The massive gates open directly into the ocean, along the coast of northern Stranglethorn Vale. Once they open, the juggernaught can sail into the Great Sea.",al={"where do the sea gates open","deadmines iron doors","exit into the ocean"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Ironclad Cove?",a="The Defias Brotherhood controls Ironclad Cove under Edwin VanCleef's command. Its hidden docks keep the juggernaught's construction secret.",al={"who runs the cove","who lives in ironclad cove"},it="residents"},{q="Who is the murloc aboard the ship?",a="The murloc is Cookie, the Defias ship's cook. Armed with a rolling pin and cooking cauldrons, he has claimed the galley as his own among the human and goblin renegades.",al={"cookie the murloc","why is there a murloc pirate","chef cookie"}},{q="What is Ironclad Cove?",a="Ironclad Cove is a vast subterranean cavern deep beneath the Deadmines, transformed into a secret shipyard. Enclosed by towering stone walls and natural waterways, it houses the docks and scaffolding where the Defias Brotherhood constructs their massive war juggernaut. A colossal reinforced door seals the cavern off from the southern seas, concealing their naval operation from the Kingdom of Stormwind until the ship is fully prepared to sail.",al={"ironclad cove info","what is this place deadmines","deadmines ship cavern"},it="place",add="dba05414"},{q="What happened at Ironclad Cove?",a="When Edwin VanCleef and his Defias Brotherhood laid claim to the Deadmines, they turned this hidden sea cavern into a secret shipyard. Behind its great sea doors they are building a massive warship, the juggernaught, out of sight of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"ironclad cove history","who had ironclad cove before","deadmines shipyard past"},it="history",add="63b814e0"},{q="Is Ironclad Cove dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. Ironclad Cove serves as the inner redoubt and nerve center of Edwin VanCleef's rebellion. The waters, catwalks, and scaffolding swarming with heavily armed Defias cutpurses, hired corsairs, goblin engineers, and deadly combatants defending their prized warship. Anyone who infiltrates this deep into the mine complex faces the most formidable commanders of the Brotherhood, determined to protect their master plan at all costs.",al={"is ironclad cove safe","ironclad cove threats","deadmines shipyard danger"},it="danger",add="3987b29d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a full-sized war galleon buried beneath Westfall makes the Defias a military threat to the Kingdom of Stormwind, far beyond a regional bandit gang.",["class:Rogue"]="For a rogue, Ironclad Cove shows the height of Edwin VanCleef's craftsmanship, engineering skill, and underground logistics. Thieves and outlaws consider it legendary."},kw={"cookie","deadmines ship","defias cove","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","shipyard"},rel={"zone:deadmines","subzone:deadmines","npc:cookie","topic:pirate","zone:stranglethorn"},src={"Ironclad Cove"}}
E["subzone:mast-room"] = {t="subzone",n="Mast Room",z="deadmines",s="Timber from Westfall reaches the Mast Room, deep in the Deadmines, where goblin woodcarvers shape it for the Defias.",h="Timber from Westfall reaches the Mast Room, deep in the Deadmines, where goblin woodcarvers shape it for the...",sec={{t="The Underground Sawmill",b="The Mast Room turns timber from Westfall into parts for a warship. Deep in the Deadmines, the cavern holds felled logs, sawdust, and great cutting machines. Goblin woodcarvers shape the masts, ribs, and planks needed for the vessel hidden farther within Ironclad Cove. Sneed watches over their work as the Defias Brotherhood makes the wood serve its war.",sp=1},{t="Industrial Labor",b="Sneed directs the goblin woodcarvers from atop a mechanical shredder. Logs rise and pass through the planers in a steady flow, while the workers meet his demanding quotas. The old gold mine now rings with the labor of a shipyard, where timber becomes the pieces of a vessel.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is there a lumber mill inside an underground mine?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is secretly building a great warship in the cove beneath the mines. The Mast Room shapes its masts, framing, and hull planks from timber smuggled in from Westfall.",al={"why timber here","why wood in deadmines","mast room purpose"},sp=1,it="purpose"},{q="Who runs the Mast Room?",a="Sneed runs the Mast Room, directing goblin woodcarvers from a lethal mechanical lumber shredder.",al={"mast room boss","who leads mast room","who is sneed"},it="residents"},{q="Why are goblins working here for the Defias?",a="Edwin VanCleef hired goblin engineers and craftsmen for expertise human stonemasons lacked. In return for gold and profit, the goblins bring heavy machinery, explosives, and shipwright skills.",al={"why are goblins in deadmines","defias goblins"},sp=1,it="ties",bt={"defias.masons"}},{q="What is the Mast Room?",a="The Mast Room is an underground lumber mill and woodworking chamber tucked deep within the Deadmines, located just past the secondary mine shafts. Operated by hired goblin craftsmen, it is dedicated to shaping timber into critical components—most notably the heavy masts and structural woodwork—needed for Edwin VanCleef's secret juggernaut docked further in the cavern.",al={"what is mast room","mast room deadmines","about mast room"},it="place",add="7bd4bec3"},{q="Why is it called the Mast Room?",a="It earned its name from its primary purpose: shaping the massive wooden timbers and tall masts required for the Defias Brotherhood's secret warship. Deep within these subterranean halls, goblin woodcarvers mill and finish raw lumber brought into the mines to construct the rigged vessels of the Brotherhood's hidden fleet.",al={"why is it called mast room","mast room name meaning","why mast room"},it="name",add="b5fbae6b"},{q="Is the Mast Room dangerous?",a="Yes. The chamber is heavily guarded by industrious Goblin Woodcarvers and overseen by Sneed, who pilots a lethal goblin shredder against trespassers. Whirling saw blades, heavy logging machinery, and well-armed Defias hirelings make traversing the chamber a hazardous endeavor for anyone who disrupts their carpentry work.",al={"is mast room dangerous","mast room dangers","threats in mast room"},it="danger",add="31a4c95c"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Sneed's goblin shredder uses crude steam-and-cog machinery, adapted from forest logging to crush intruders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Timber from this chamber shows that Defias pillaging across Westfall serves a coordinated industrial effort."},kw={"deadmines","goblin woodcarver","lumber mill","mast room","shredder","sneed"},rel={"npc:sneed","zone:deadmines","topic:goblin"},src={"Mast Room"}}
E["zone:deadmines"] = {t="dungeon",n="The Deadmines",z="deadmines",s="Beneath Moonbrook, the Deadmines hide the Defias Brotherhood's staging ground. Once a source of the kingdom’s gold, the tunnels were abandoned in the First War and long feared as haunted. Edwin VanCleef and goblin engineers now work there beyond the realm’s eyes, building an engine of vengeance against Stormwind.",h="Beneath Moonbrook, the Deadmines hide the Defias Brotherhood's staging ground.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Gold and Ruin",b="Before the First War, the Deadmines were called the greatest gold-producing center in human lands. Their gold supplied a third of Stormwind’s reserves. When the Orcish Horde swept through the kingdom and razed the capital, the mines were hastily abandoned to darkness.\n\nSir Anduin Lothar spent twenty months imprisoned by subterranean ogres while recovering the sacred Tome of Divinity. Warchief Blackhand’s rebellious daughter Griselda fled into the lower passages with the ogre Turok, and both met their ends there. Believed cursed and home only to shambling undead and lurking subterranean vermin, the depths lay untouched for decades.",sp=0},{t="Sanctum of the Brotherhood",b="After the Stonemasons’ Guild was cast out of Stormwind without payment for rebuilding the city, Edwin VanCleef gathered the disgruntled artisans into the Defias Brotherhood. Seeking a secure headquarters beyond the reach of Gryan Stoutmantle’s People’s Militia, the Brotherhood chose its central redoubt in the abandoned tunnels.\n\nThey drove out the legitimate Miners’ League, leaving Foreman Thistlenettle’s doomed workers to perish and rise as undead ghouls. Lumbering ogres, seasoned brigands, and mechanical constructs guard the shafts, now an industrial war camp. Picks, fires, and illicit industry echo through the lower mines once more.",sp=0},{t="The Secret of Ironclad Cove",b="Beyond the sweltering Goblin Foundry and timber-strewn Mast Room, Ironclad Cove opens beneath the Dagger Hills. There, VanCleef employed goblin shipbuilders and tinkerers to construct a colossal ironclad dreadnaught. Captain Greenskin commands the warship, with First Mate Mr. Smite beside him.\n\nThe ship is designed to pass through an underwater sea gate toward the ocean. There, the Defias Brotherhood means to prey on the sea trade that keeps Stormwind rich.",sp=1,bt={"defias.juggernaut"}}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to the Deadmines located?",a="The entrance lies inside a derelict barn in ruined Moonbrook, southwestern Westfall. Winding tunnels cross an outer complex of Defias diggers and undead miners before reaching the locked instance threshold.",al={"deadmines entrance","how to get to deadmines","where is deadmines"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does everyone call the Deadmines 'VC'?",a="Adventurers call the dungeon “VC” after its master, Edwin VanCleef. The shorthand avoids confusion with Dire Maul in Feralas, an ancient elven complex that shares the initials “DM.”",al={"why vc","vc meaning","why call it vc"},it="name"},{q="Who is Edwin VanCleef?",a="Edwin VanCleef was the brilliant guildmaster of the Stonemasons, who oversaw Stormwind City’s majestic reconstruction after the First War. When the House of Nobles refused to pay its debts, VanCleef formed the Defias Brotherhood to demand restitution through rebellion and open brigandage.",al={"vancleef backstory","who is the final boss","defias leader"},it="leader"},{q="What is being built in Ironclad Cove?",a="The Defias are building a massive ironclad juggernaut in Ironclad Cove. They contracted goblin engineers to assemble it with heavy ordnance and sturdy timber, so it can sail through the cove’s sea gate and raid the trade that feeds the capital.",al={"what are they building","deadmines ship","juggernaught"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the Miners' League workers outside the instance?",a="Foreman Thistlenettle and his crew were sent to legally reopen the mines for the kingdom. When the Defias stormed the works, a tunnel collapse trapped the miners in the dark. They starved there and eventually rose as mindless, restless undead.",al={"thistlenettle fate","why are there undead miners","collecting memories lore"},it="history"},{q="What does defeating Cookie the murloc mean for the Defias ship?",a="Cookie is the bizarre ship’s cook aboard VanCleef’s dreadnaught. Defeating VanCleef cuts off the rebellion’s head. Slaying Cookie clears the remaining crew from the ship’s galley and breaks the crew’s presence in Ironclad Cove before you escape through the coastal passage.",al={"cookie the murloc","why is cookie a boss","cookie deadmines"}},{q="Where does the exit tunnel lead when leaving the dungeon?",a="The natural tunnel behind the dreadnaught leads to an exit along the coastal bluffs of the Dagger Hills. From there, you look out toward the ocean and the Westfall Lighthouse.",al={"deadmines exit","where does the exit go"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Deadmines?",a="The Deadmines are a sprawling network of labyrinthine tunnels carved deep beneath Westfall and northwestern Stranglethorn Vale. Before the First War, they were the richest gold-producing center in human lands, said to have held a third of Stormwind's entire treasure reserves. They were abandoned when the Horde invaded and sacked the kingdom, leaving the shafts deserted for years until outlaw hands claimed them.",al={"what is the deadmines","deadmines history","tell me about the deadmines"},it="place",add="d03732b9",nx={9,10}},{q="Why is it called the Deadmines?",a="After the First War brought devastation and ruin to Stormwind, the abandoned gold shafts fell into dark disuse and were widely believed to be haunted. Between the deadly horrors that prowled their depths and the silence of an exhausted, forsaken realm of stone, travelers began referring to the forsaken pits simply as the Deadmines.",al={"why deadmines named","why called deadmines","deadmines name origin"},it="name",add="990a0946"},{q="Who dug these tunnels?",a="Generations of human laborers and guildsmen extracted fortunes of gold from these hills to fuel Stormwind's early expansion. More recently, the Miners' League attempted to reopen the pits under Foreman Thistlenettle, only for the Defias Brotherhood and their conscripted diggers to seize the subterranean network and carve out extensive fortifications of their own.",al={"who built deadmines","who dug deadmines","miners who made deadmines"},it="origin",add="001f20c6"},{q="Who are the Defias Brotherhood?",a="The Defias Brotherhood is a ruthless order of renegades, bandits, and outlaws made up of former stonemasons, thieves, highwaymen, and cutthroats. Sworn enemies of the kingdom, they have taken control of Westfall and operate from the shadows, plotting to exact bloody vengeance and tear down the ruling nobility of Stormwind.",al={"who are the defias","defias brotherhood","what is defias"},it="threat",add="b6ffba12",nx={12,13}},{q="Why do they wear red bandanas?",a="The Defias wear red silk bandanas as a defiant symbol of the blood shed by the oppressed working class of Stormwind. It marks their allegiance to Edwin VanCleef's rebellion and reminds every member of the debt of blood they believe the royal court owes them.",al={"why red bandanas","defias red masks","meaning of red bandana"},it="identity",add="d563a934"},{q="Who started the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Edwin VanCleef, the former Guildmaster of the Stonemasons Guild, founded the Brotherhood. After spending years rebuilding the shattered ramparts of Stormwind, he turned his extensive training in stealth, subterfuge, and engineering toward open insurrection when the kingdom's aristocracy refused to pay his workers.",al={"who founded defias","who started brotherhood","defias founder"},it="leader",add="29fe0b04"},{q="Why are the Defias hiding in an old mine?",a="The Deadmines offer a massive, defensible fortress hidden beneath the quiet ruins of Moonbrook. With Westfall largely abandoned by the royal army and the tunnels' forgotten subterranean chambers connecting directly to a concealed ocean cove, VanCleef found the perfect secluded staging ground to amass an army and heavy weaponry undisturbed.",al={"why deadmines hideout","why defias in mine","why hide in deadmines"},it="purpose",add="90ba82c0",nx={15}},{q="Is there really a ship in the mine?",a="Yes. At the deepest point of the labyrinth lies Ironclad Cove, a colossal underground subterranean basin. Anchored there is a massive iron-plated war juggernaught, fitted with heavy cannons and rigged by goblin engineers, ready to sail through a hidden sea gate into the ocean once completed.",al={"is there a ship in deadmines","deadmines juggernaught","defias warship"},it="threat",add="019c688c"},{q="Who's in charge down here?",a="Edwin VanCleef commands the entirety of the operation from his cabin aboard the warship deep in Ironclad Cove. From this subterranean perch, he directs the mining, engineering, and raiding operations that grip Westfall.",al={"who leads deadmines","who runs deadmines","deadmines boss"},it="in_charge",add="763d2dd2",nx={17,18}},{q="Does VanCleef have lieutenants?",a="He commands a diverse cabal of trusted enforcers throughout the shafts. The brutish ogre Rhahk'Zor guards the upper gates, Sneed commands the lumber workshops from within an iron shredder, the goblin Gilnid runs the foundry smelters, and Captain Greenskin alongside the ruthless tauren first mate, Mr. Smite, oversee the juggernaught.",al={"vancleef officers","deadmines commanders","defias lieutenants"},it="allies",add="985d6768"},{q="Who are the goblins working for?",a="The goblins work directly under Edwin VanCleef as hired specialists and mercenary craftsmen. Operating the foundry, timber workshops, and shipyards, they bring the technical mastery and industrial machinery needed to construct VanCleef's warmachines in exchange for coin, influence, and resources.",al={"who hired the goblins","are goblins defias","goblin alliance defias"},it="ties",add="27e06e7a"},{q="Why did they send me to kill their leader?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the beleaguered People's Militia lack the military strength to breach the Deadmines themselves. With Stormwind turning a blind eye and dismissing the threat, the militia relies entirely on brave, independent adventurers like you to strike deep into the mountain and sever the head of the serpent.",al={"why send me kill vancleef","gryan stoutmantle request","why kill defias leader"},it="why_me",add="fb90d257",nx={20,21}},{q="Has anyone else tried to kill VanCleef?",a="Not successfully. Stormwind has sent no army against him, and the People's Militia at Sentinel Hill lacks the strength to storm the mines, which is why Gryan Stoutmantle turns to adventurers.",al={"who tried to kill vancleef","past deadmines invasions","did anyone attack deadmines"},it="history",add="e11d0994"},{q="Why can't the Stormwind army do it?",a="Stormwind's standing forces are stretched thin across Elwynn and distant borders, crippled by debts and bureaucratic apathy. The House of Nobles refuses to fund an expedition to Westfall, leaving the provincial farms undefended and forcing the volunteer People's Militia to handle the crisis alone.",al={"why no stormwind army","why doesnt stormwind clear deadmines","stormwind guards westfall"},it="conflict",add="22846885"},{q="How did the Defias take over the mines?",a="After escaping Stormwind, VanCleef led his followers into the lawless fields of Westfall. They ambushed the local mining operations, collapsed key tunnels to trap royal workers, and fortified the vast underground network into an impregnable base of operations.",al={"how defias took deadmines","how deadmines fell","defias mine takeover"},it="history",add="93f204fb",nx={23}},{q="Did the miners join the Defias?",a="While the Miners' League workers were ambushed and perished, many disenfranchised laborers, cutpurses, and desperate vagrants willingly joined the Brotherhood's cause. Today, non-elite laborers and strip miners toil endlessly in the shafts under the watchful whips of Defias overseers and taskmasters.",al={"did miners become defias","are miners defias","miners working for defias"},it="residents",add="9fd39a6b"},{q="Why are there goblins down here helping the Defias?",a="Building an armored juggernaught and complex harvest watchers requires advanced metallurgical and mechanical expertise that common bandits lack. VanCleef contracted goblin engineers, craftsmen, and lumber carvers, who happily established foundries and workshops inside the caverns in exchange for wealth and profit.",al={"why goblins deadmines","goblin presence deadmines","why are goblins here"},it="threat",add="a6aef884",nx={25,26}},{q="What do the goblins get out of helping the Defias?",a="For the goblins, it is strictly business. They receive a massive cut of gold looted from Westfall's mines, unchecked access to high-grade ore and lumber, and total freedom to test volatile engineering prototypes away from trade prince jurisdiction.",al={"what do goblins get","goblin profit deadmines","why do goblins work for defias"},it="motive",add="b9fb938c"},{q="Who is Sneed?",a="Sneed is a cunning goblin supervisor who oversees the Defias lumber operation in the Mast Room. He commands the timber cutting from inside a heavy, razor-edged lumber Shredder, carving massive trees into masts and beams for the dreadnaught.",al={"who is sneed","sneed deadmines","sneed boss"},it="identity",add="4854becf"},{q="What is this Stonemasons Guild everyone keeps talking about?",a="The Stonemasons Guild was the esteemed union of architects, masons, and craftsmen led by Edwin VanCleef that rebuilt Stormwind City from ruins following its sacking in the First War. They restored its white ramparts and towers, only to become the foundation of the rebellion when kingdom politics betrayed them.",al={"stonemasons guild","what was the stonemasons guild","who were the stonemasons"},it="history",add="ba2c808f",nx={28,29}},{q="Did Stormwind really refuse to pay the Stonemasons?",a="Yes. Stormwind's House of Nobles ran up catastrophic debts expanding military campaigns and refused to provide the full compensation promised for rebuilding the city. Manipulated in secret by Lady Katrana Prestor, the nobility offered only meager payouts and abruptly dissolved the Guild when VanCleef demanded restitution.",al={"did stormwind not pay stonemasons","why werent stonemasons paid","house of nobles payment stonemasons"},sp=1,it="conflict",add="30bf5c0b",bt={"prestor.onyxia"}},{q="Was there a riot in Stormwind?",a="When the guild was disbanded without pay, VanCleef led furious riots through the streets of Stormwind. The Crown cracked down harshly, driving the rebellious artisans out into exile.",al={"stormwind riot stonemasons","what happened in the stonemason riot"},sp=1,it="history",add="6779ccff"},{q="Are the Defias just bandits or something worse?",a="They are far more than common thieves. The Defias Brotherhood is a organized, deeply entrenched revolutionary syndicate wielding advanced goblin engineering, espionage, and trained magic, all driven by a personal and ideological hatred of Stormwind's ruling class.",al={"are defias bandits","how dangerous are defias","defias threat level"},it="threat",add="8f04eff1",nx={31,32}},{q="Do the Defias have an actual plan?",a="Their goal is nothing short of bringing Stormwind to its knees. By stripping Westfall of resources and starving the capital, while secretly building a heavy iron warship beneath the earth, they intend to sail directly to Stormwind Keep and bombard the kingdom into unconditional surrender.",al={"defias master plan","what is defias goal","what do defias want"},sp=1,it="purpose",add="2dd70853"},{q="Could the Defias threaten Stormwind itself?",a="Very much so. With King Varian missing, the court paralyzed by internal intrigue, and the royal army stretched past its limit, a surprise naval assault from a fully armed iron juggernaught could shatter Stormwind's harbor defenses and leave the city defenseless from within.",al={"can defias destroy stormwind","could defias take stormwind","threat to stormwind defias"},sp=1,it="danger",add="9ff64ec1"},{q="What happens after VanCleef is dead?",a="Delivering VanCleef's severed head to Gryan Stoutmantle at Sentinel Hill confirms the mastermind's demise, dealing a staggering blow to the Brotherhood's grand campaign. Furthermore, documents found upon his corpse, such as an unsent letter, point toward deeper conspiracies and corruption festering in the very heart of Stormwind.",al={"after vancleef dies","vancleef dead what next","fallout of vancleef death"},sp=1,it="next_step",add="9d82770e",nx={34,35}},{q="Does killing VanCleef end the Defias?",a="It shatters their immediate plans, but it does not eradicate the rebellion. Thousands of cutpurses, brigands, and sympathizers remain entrenched across Westfall, Redridge, and the Stockades, harboring bitter hatred toward the crown that outlives their founding kingpin.",al={"does defias end with vancleef","is defias defeated","does vancleef death stop defias"},sp=1,it="threat",add="f607b8be"},{q="Will Westfall finally be safe after VanCleef falls?",a="Not immediately. Rogue mechanical harvest watchers still stalk the blighted fields, gnoll packs prowl the hills, and scattered Defias cells continue to plunder farms. The People's Militia will have a long, uphill struggle before peace ever truly returns to the plains.",al={"is westfall safe now","will westfall recover","westfall after deadmines"},sp=1,it="today",add="c2558e80"},{q="Why is Westfall such a mess?",a="Westfall was once the fertile breadbasket of the kingdom, but years of neglect, droughts, and Defias terror reduced it to ruin. Outlaws ran off the homesteaders, seized the mines, and left the once-lush pastures fallow and infested with ravenous scavengers and rogue harvest golems.",al={"why is westfall ruined","what happened to westfall","westfall state of affairs"},it="arrival",add="d15c407d",nx={37,38}},{q="Where did all the Westfall farmers go?",a="Most were violently driven from their land when the Defias overran the countryside, fleeing to the gates of Sentinel Hill or begging on the streets of Stormwind. Only a handful of stubborn homesteaders remain on their family plots, desperately fighting off bandits and gnolls to scrape together a harvest.",al={"where are the farmers","what happened to westfall farmers","displaced westfall farmers"},it="residents",add="8c3ab485"},{q="Why doesn't the king send help to Westfall?",a="King Varian Wrynn has mysteriously vanished, leaving his young son Anduin and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon to oversee the realm. The royal court, manipulated by squabbling nobles, claims the kingdom has insufficient funds and military manpower to spare for Westfall's defense, abandoning the province to its own devices.",al={"why doesnt the king help westfall","why no help from king","king varian westfall help"},sp=1,it="conflict",add="619c91ff"},{q="How did I end up in The Deadmines?",a="Your hunt for the Defias Brotherhood led you across the blighted plains of Westfall to Moonbrook, an abandoned town overrun by brigands. A Defias traitor helped you pinpoint their secret headquarters hidden within the dilapidated mine entrance on the edge of town. Fighting your way down through the old mining tunnels and past undead excavations, you breached the depths where the Brotherhood has made its fortified lair.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","how do i get in here"},it="arrival",add="21f940b9"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in The Deadmines?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia sent you to cut the head off the snake. You are here to fight through the Brotherhood's miners, goblin tinkerers, and pirate mercenaries to reach Ironclad Cove. Once there, you must board their warship, confront Edwin VanCleef himself, and claim his head to break the Defias hold over Westfall once and for all.",al={"what am i doing here","what is my goal here","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="a22369d2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Deadmines are Stormwind’s gravest internal threat. Bringing down VanCleef is the defining victory that restores hope to Westfall’s besieged farmers.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a test of valor and faith in these desecrated shafts. They echo the historic trials of Sir Anduin Lothar and the lost miners whose restless dead still wander the outer tunnels.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you find rocky tunnels that once supplied a third of the capital’s wealth. Veins of copper, tin, and precious silver still run through them.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study the Goblin Foundry and Sneed’s mechanical workshop. They show cutting-edge steam shredders, remote-controlled golems, and specialized ordnance."},kw={"cookie","deadmines","defias","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","moonbrook","mr. smite","vancleef","westfall"},rel={"topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:edwin-vancleef","zone:westfall","subzone:moonbrook","subzone:ironclad-cove","npc:mr-smite","quest:65","quest:373"},m={levels="17-26"},src={"Deadmines (Classic)","Deadmines"}}
